DECISION MergeRulesHaveOnePublicHome
	SPEC "The corpus is the single public source of the merge rules, one RULE DOMAIN merge per"
		+ "conflict the merge settles"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/rules.awawa"
	SPEC "The README does not restate the merge rules and carries an index naming the rule entity"
		+ "that settles each topic"
		IMPL "README.md::This README deliberately does not restate the"
	SPEC "The JSON schemas are documented in English, their title and description being public"
		+ "documentation"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas"
	SPEC "The global save file schema is kept as the formal description of the format, although no"
		+ "code consumes it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/save-file.schema.json"
	REJECTED "Correcting the duplication instead of removing it"
	REJECTED "Keeping docs/game-rules.md as the public home once each of its thirty GR-* rules had"
		+ "become a SPEC of a RULE entity: the document would have been a second copy of the"
		+ "corpus, maintained by hand, which is the duplication this ruling exists to end"
	RATIONALE "The duplication is what had let the README claim a union of players by identifier,"
		+ "shared planets that were not implemented and statistics reduced to a single field"
	SOURCE "Pull request #42"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST42

DECISION WorldObjectNamesAreAttestedBySourceOrSave
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "A world object name is kept only when it is attested by the label file used as the"
		+ "inventory of group identifiers, or read in one of the reference saves"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/worldObjectNames.ts::labels-engplus.txt"
	SPEC "A group identifier is identified against that file, never by the resemblance of a name to"
		+ "a wiki page title"
		IMPL "docs/energy-levels.md"
	SPEC "The repository labels are not replaced by those of that source"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.json"
	SPEC "The label table and the name list constrain each other: a label without a name and a name"
		+ "without a label both fail the label spec"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.spec.ts::should find a label"
			+ "for each of them"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.spec.ts::should label no"
			+ "name the game is not known to use"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/worldObjectNames.ts"
	SPEC "The provenance of the identifiers is documented outside the code"
		IMPL "docs/energy-levels.md::labels-engplus.txt"
	REJECTED "Identifying a group identifier by resemblance to a wiki page title"
	REJECTED "Replacing the repository labels with those of the attestation source"
	RATIONALE "The identification rule avoided three data errors, each giving a machine the value"
		+ "of another. The source is the label file of a community mod: its labels are"
		+ "community-made, but its keys are the game's group identifiers, since a translation file"
		+ "resolves no other way in game; that distinction allows using it for the inventory and"
		+ "forbids using it for the labels. Our labels disambiguate names the game repeats and"
		+ "carry information the source does not print. The label table was built by spreading"
		+ "constant objects, which disables the excess property check: it held 33 keys typed"
		+ "nowhere"
	SOURCE "Decided in the review of pull request #43"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST43

DECISION ACaseDuplicatedKeyIsSettledByAttestation
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "Of the two keys Keycard1 and KeyCard1, both labelled Access card, only Keycard1 remains,"
		+ "in the label table as in the name union"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.json::Keycard1"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/worldObjectNames.ts::'Keycard1'"
	SPEC "KeyCard2 keeps its case: the game itself mixes the case between item 1 and item 2, and"
		+ "that form is the attested one"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.json::KeyCard2"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/worldObjectNames.ts::'KeyCard2'"
	REJECTED "Keeping both keys: the union would stay permissive to a spelling no save attests"
	REJECTED "Removing only the label: the domain would then accept a name without a presentation"
		+ "label, which the cross constraint of the two tables forbids"
	RATIONALE "This applies the attestation rule to a key duplicated by case alone. Measured on the"
		+ "four reference saves: Keycard1 is attested 156, 152 and 80 times in three of them,"
		+ "KeyCard1 in none, KeyCard2 136, 152 and 71 times in the same three. The two keys are"
		+ "distinct for TypeScript, so the type-check says nothing of a duplicate whose two members"
		+ "carry the same label"
		REF @DECISION.WorldObjectNamesAreAttestedBySourceOrSave
	SOURCE "User ruling, pull request #76"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST76

DECISION AnErrorsOriginDecidesItsPath
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "An error on an input file the tool does not modify belongs to validation, which runs"
		+ "first; the same error arising later is a broken invariant and fails loudly"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors"
	SPEC "An error the tool creates through its own intervention (merge, renumbering,"
		+ "serialization, writing) reaches the UI and the CLI through a presenter outcome in"
		+ "business language, never through an exception"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::this.presenter.presentMergedSaveUnusable()"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages/mergeFailureMessages.js::mergedSaveUnusableMessage"
	SPEC "Each error family has its own presenter outcome, never a generic one"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/MergeResultPresenterPort.ts::presentMergedSaveUnusable"
	SPEC "The catch is typed on the domain error, never on unknown: everything else keeps"
		+ "propagating as an exception"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts"
	SPEC "The invariants of the core-mapping infrastructure live in a directory of named errors"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors"
	REJECTED "A generic presenter outcome carrying any error"
	REJECTED "Converting every caught error into an outcome, whatever its family"
	REJECTED "Letting an error born of the tool's own intervention propagate as an exception"
	RATIONALE "Reusing the input files outcome would tell the user their saves are bad when the"
		+ "tool is what failed. A parse error met by the merger concerns the two input files that"
		+ "validation accepted one line earlier: it is a broken invariant, and no presenter outcome"
		+ "is added for it. What the user sees of a corrupted save stays the validation refusal,"
		+ "before any merge and any writing"
	SOURCE "Decided in the review of pull request #47; its second half delivered by pull requests"
		+ "#54 and #59"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST47
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST54
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST59

DECISION ABrokenInvariantFailsWithANamedErrorType
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "A broken invariant of the core-mapping infrastructure fails with a named error type,"
		+ "never with a bare Error"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors/UnexpectedSaveSectionError.ts::extends"
			+ "Error"
	SPEC "Each invariant of the layer has its type in the errors directory"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors"
	SPEC "The JSDoc of the error carries the instruction, not only the cause: fix what let the data"
		+ "through, never soften the guard"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors/UnexpectedSaveSectionError.ts::never"
			+ "soften the guard"
	SPEC "A section expected as an array that is not one raises"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/errors/UnexpectedSaveSectionError.ts::should"
			+ "hold a list of entries"
	REJECTED "Throwing a bare Error and telling the cases apart by their message"
	REJECTED "A silent fallback on the shape of the section"
	RATIONALE "The invariants of one layer must be caught and told apart from a programming bug in"
		+ "the same way; the spec checks the type, then the message. The silent fallback that"
		+ "discarded a malformed section by its shape is what had left a whole section unvalidated."
		+ "The scope is this layer: the other packages keep their bare Error as long as they have"
		+ "neither an errors directory nor a second case to align"
	SOURCE "Decided in the review of pull request #48"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST48

DECISION ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "The validation result carries the warnings, never the parser"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveValidationResult.ts::warnings:"
			+ "SaveWarningCode[]"
	SPEC "The parsing port declares no warnings field"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveSectionsParserPort.ts::the single"
			+ "source of warnings"
	SPEC "Validation runs first in the four flows (display, merge in the UI, merge on the command"
		+ "line, validation on the command line), and warnings are reported on every outcome,"
		+ "invalid saves and successful merges included"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application"
	REJECTED "Having the parsing port carry the warnings"
	RATIONALE "Two producers of warnings means two lists to reconcile in every consumer, and a flow"
		+ "that forgets one"
	SOURCE "Decided on 2026-09-06"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION UserTextLivesInCoreMappingPresentation
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "An internal code (warning, merge failure) is turned into a sentence by the core-mapping"
		+ "presentation; the ViewModel exposes strings ready to display"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatSaveWarning.ts"
	SPEC "The user-facing sentences of core-mapping live in a single directory"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages"
	SPEC "An outcome that carries no text has its fixed sentence in the messages directory; an"
		+ "outcome that already carries its messages gets no additional one"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages/mergeFailureMessages.js::mergedSaveUnusableMessage"
	SPEC "An unknown code falls back to a generic message, and the code itself is never displayed"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatSaveWarning.ts::unknownSaveWarningMessage"
	REJECTED "Translating the codes in the UI"
	REJECTED "Displaying the internal code when no sentence exists"
	REJECTED "Giving an accompanying sentence to an outcome that already carries its messages"
	RATIONALE "Translating in the UI would duplicate the table for the CLI and put domain knowledge"
		+ "into a delivery mechanism. One more fixed label in the ViewModel, when the outcome"
		+ "already carries its messages, would double the title each delivery mechanism already"
		+ "writes"
	SOURCE "Decided on 2026-09-06; completed by pull requests #54 and #59"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST54
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST59

DECISION ALocationIsABusinessLabelFollowedByTheIndex
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "A validation message travels as a message and a location, the location being null when"
		+ "the error concerns the whole file"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatValidationIssue.ts"
	SPEC "The location is a business label followed by the index; the entry segment disappears when"
		+ "the error targets no entry, and a section missing from the table falls back to its"
		+ "number"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatErrorLocation.ts"
	SPEC "The location is formatted in presentation, next to the other message formatters; the"
		+ "ViewModel never exposes the raw indexes"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatErrorLocation.ts"
	SPEC "A warning and an error share the same ViewModel: only the field that carries them tells"
		+ "which severity it is"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/viewModels"
	SPEC "The section label table is complete, and an exhaustiveness test fails as soon as a"
		+ "section is missing from it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages/saveSectionLabels.js::export const"
			+ "saveSectionLabels"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatErrorLocation.spec.ts::When the"
			+ "section has no label"
	REJECTED "The index alone, which is a detail of the file format"
	REJECTED "The label alone, too poor to edit the save by hand"
	REJECTED "Keeping the raw indexes in the ViewModel"
	RATIONALE "The label is for understanding, the index for finding the section in a text editor."
		+ "Keeping the raw indexes in the ViewModel would force the CLI and the UI to call the"
		+ "formatter themselves, hence to export it from core-mapping, which the exports rule"
		+ "forbids. Message and location stay two distinct fields: each delivery mechanism chooses"
		+ "whether to display the location, and where"
	SOURCE "Pull request #37"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST37

DECISION BothMessageListsShareOneRendering
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "A single component renders both lists"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/validation/ValidationMessagesList.tsx"
	SPEC "The distinction between errors and warnings is carried by the separation of the two"
		+ "lists, never by a parameter of the component"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/validation/ValidationMessagesList.tsx"
	SPEC "A validation message reads as a stack frame: the whole item in monospace, the message on"
		+ "the first line, its origin below, prefixed and indented, in a tone one step fainter than"
		+ "the message"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/validation/ValidationMessagesList.tsx"
	SPEC "The word that introduces the origin lives in the UI messages; the layout is in CSS, and"
		+ "core-mapping knows nothing of the rendering"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/validationMessages.js::validationMessageLocationPrefix"
	REJECTED "Parameterizing the list component by severity"
	REJECTED "Placing the location before the message"
	RATIONALE "Collapsible and monospace is not an option offered to the consumer: it is the single"
		+ "rendering of both lists, and the parameters that had opened it were removed. The first"
		+ "form, location before the message in faded text outside the code block, was refused in"
		+ "review on a screenshot: two typefaces on one line. The chosen form also settles the"
		+ "order, a stack putting the message first"
	SOURCE "Decided in the review of pull request #37"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST37

DECISION UiSaveManagerHasOneUiErrorIdiom
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "A controller call that does not complete sets a local error signal, logs the technical"
		+ "detail, and displays a fixed sentence living in the package messages"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/MergeSection.tsx::console.error(error)"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/lib/useLoadSaveFile.ts::console.error(error)"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/mergeSectionMessages.js::mergeSectionCallFailedMessage"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/displayRouteMessages.js::displayRouteCallFailedMessage"
	SPEC "The failure notice is displayed next to the input fields, under the button that produced"
		+ "it, never in the area reserved for what a successful parse produced"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/MergeSection.tsx"
	SPEC "The two UI flows share the mechanism, the naming and the placement"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src"
	SPEC "The presenter outcome says what the operation decided and the UI signal says the call did"
		+ "not complete; the two mechanisms coexist without overlapping"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src"
	REJECTED "Placing the failure notice where the validation messages go"
	REJECTED "Leaving a bare catch that logs nothing"
	RATIONALE "User ruling: placing the notice in the visualization area put it about 670 px under"
		+ "the button that produced it, hence off screen on a short window, and made it look like a"
		+ "parse result. The bare catch without logging was an omission, not a ruling: none of the"
		+ "three places where a justification would have lived mentions one"
	SOURCE "Pull request #58; placement ruled in review"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST58

DECISION ADomainRuleIgnoresValidationVocabulary
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "No file of the domain imports application"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain"
	SPEC "A domain rule returns a failure type it declares itself, without code or sentence;"
		+ "validateUniqueHost returns that type, or null when the invariant holds"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/validateUniqueHost.ts::UniqueHostViolation |"
			+ "null"
	SPEC "The infrastructure translates that type into a validation issue, attaching the code and"
		+ "the detail sentence"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateSaveContent.js::function"
			+ "toUniqueHostIssue"
	SPEC "The six issue codes stay in application and are all attached from the infrastructure"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/ValidationIssue.ts"
	REJECTED "A generic domain violation type carrying a rule discriminant: it brings back into the"
		+ "domain the code vocabulary meant to leave it, for a single rule"
	REJECTED "Moving ValidationIssue and its codes down into the domain: it would carry there a"
		+ "vocabulary of technical errors (invalid-extension, invalid-json, schema-violation) with"
		+ "no business meaning"
	REJECTED "Throwing InvalidSaveDataError from the rule: validation would stop being exhaustive,"
		+ "the first defect hiding the next ones"
	RATIONALE "Exactly one host is a business invariant: the rule stays in the domain, only its"
		+ "error vocabulary leaves it"
	SOURCE "User ruling at the launch of part A of the core-mapping domain boundaries task, pull"
		+ "request #62"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST62

DECISION SectionCountersAreDeclaredOnceWithNamedIndexes
	SPEC "The section and part counters are declared once, and each index carries a name"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/sectionIndexes.js"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/verifySectionCount.js"
	SPEC "Internal constants that count 10 sections plus a reserved part describe the arithmetic,"
		+ "not the format, and keep their names"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/sectionIndexes.js::SAVE_SPLIT_PARTS_COUNT"
	REJECTED "Renaming to parts and data sections: section is the word of the public vocabulary"
	REJECTED "Letting each module count its own way under its own name"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.ASaveHasElevenSectionsTheLastReservedAndEmpty
	RATIONALE "One count everywhere: it is what save-file.schema.json declares, what the user"
		+ "message Expected 11 sections counts and what the parser returns; three competing"
		+ "vocabularies had let the README state something other than the code. The legacy format"
		+ "counts 11 real sections, a numeric namesake of the 11 parts of the current format, so"
		+ "the counters carry names that say sections of a save and parts"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-07, names settled in the review of pull request 47"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST47

DECISION OneModuleAloneParsesASaveLine
	SPEC "The parser is the only point of production code where a save line reaches JSON.parse;"
		+ "validation and merge both use it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js"
	SPEC "Failure is per line and located: each failing line is reported alone, without taking down"
		+ "the valid entries around it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js"
	SPEC "An empty section stays empty and produces no error"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js"
	REJECTED "Keeping a second parser in the validator"
	REJECTED "A non-lazy variant of the parser: it reopens the door this decision closes"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.ASectionLineIsOneJsonEntry
	RATIONALE "Two implementations tolerating the same format differently are a defect in their own"
		+ "right, whatever bug they produce: that divergence made the defect of pull request 34"
		+ "silent, validation declaring the save valid while the merge lost a whole section. The"
		+ "world objects section is returned as a generator factory, one entry at a time instead of"
		+ "the 28425 objects of a reference save materialized"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-09, pull request 47, confirmed in review"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST47

DECISION AnInt64IdentifierIsCarriedByItsDecimalText
	SPEC "An identifier of the save format beyond the exact integer range of a double is carried by"
		+ "its exact decimal text, never by a number"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/int64Identifiers.js::keepInt64IdentifierText"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/serializeSave.spec.js::When a save holding an"
			+ "int64 player identifier is read back"
	SPEC "The rule targets the format, not a field: any future int64 field follows it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/int64Identifiers.js::RAW_INTEGER_FIELDS"
	SPEC "Exactness is produced and consumed in shared-save-processing alone, and the schema of the"
		+ "section concerned declares a decimal string"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js::keepInt64IdentifierText"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section2-players.schema.json::Player Steam ID"
			+ "(primary key, int64)"
	SPEC "The list of int64 fields, the emission test and the reviver live in a single module"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/int64Identifiers.js"
	REJECTED "Restating the rule in a public markdown document: the obligation existed only to keep"
		+ "that copy in step with the code, and the rule is now a corpus entity this ruling names"
		+ "through RESTS_ON"
	REJECTED "Typing the field as BigInt: JSON.stringify throws on it, ajv cannot validate it, and"
		+ "it announces arithmetic the project never does"
	REJECTED "Keeping the raw text of the section entries: the merge rebuilds every player entry"
	REJECTED "Setting a validation rule on integer precision"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.ThePlayerIdentifierIsTheOnlyInt64FieldBeyondDoubleRange
	RESTS_ON @RULE.APlayerIdentifierIsCarriedAsExactDecimalText
	RATIONALE "The source text of a JSON literal is read through the third parameter of the reviver"
		+ "(ES2025), supported on the three engines the UI scenarios target, which all return the"
		+ "literal intact where the parsed value rounds. The reviver applies to the players section"
		+ "only: applying it everywhere would send the 115838 key/value pairs of the world objects"
		+ "section through a function call for a field that does not exist there. No validation"
		+ "rule bears on integer precision, a large literal in a save being normal: the guard is a"
		+ "round-trip test and the type system, which makes a numeric fixture impossible"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-07, delivered by pull request 49"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST49

DECISION TheFloatSuffixIsAppliedAtEmission
	SPEC "The .0 suffix of float fields is applied at emission, in a field-by-field serialization"
		+ "of the entry, never by textual post-processing of the produced string"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/stringifyEntry.js::export function stringifyEntry"
	SPEC "A non-flat entry throws instead of being serialized silently"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/stringifyEntry.js::save entries are expected to be"
			+ "flat"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/shared-save-processing/stringifyEntry.spec.js::When a field holds a"
			+ "nested value"
	REJECTED "A textual post-processing of the produced string"
	REJECTED "Narrowing the parameter type instead of keeping the runtime check: the type states"
		+ "the contract only for type-checked callers"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
	RATIONALE "A textual sentinel rewrites any string value carrying its pattern: a sign whose"
		+ "player text was FLOAT:5 came out as a number. Silence was the real risk: where a reviver"
		+ "applied the suffix at any depth, field-by-field emission handles the first level only,"
		+ "and a nested entry would come out without a suffix and without any sign. The instruction"
		+ "carried by the JSDoc of the error is to fix what passed a nested entry, or to extend the"
		+ "module to deeper levels, never to loosen the guard"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-07, pull request 36, guard added in review"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST36

DECISION ASchemaRuleHoldsByMeaningBeforeMeasurement
	SPEC "Every bound or schema rule holds by meaning before holding by measurement; only"
		+ "implications that hold by meaning are written, never one holding by a coincidence of"
		+ "group identifier"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section3-world-objects.schema.json::\"dependencies\""
	SPEC "additionalProperties stays closed: the format is described exhaustively"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/section3-world-objects.schema.json::\"additionalProperties\":"
			+ "false"
	SPEC "The ten section schemas stay in draft-07 and express their implications with the"
		+ "dependencies keyword in array form"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas"
	REJECTED "Fixing two lines so that the reference saves pass: it would freeze on a sample what"
		+ "must be understood"
	REJECTED "Deducing a missing value from a regularity observed between tiers"
	RATIONALE "A bound set on the sample alone will refuse a legitimate save tomorrow. The survey"
		+ "of 2026-09-09 on ten saves and 190338 world objects attests only two universal"
		+ "properties; the eighteen others range from 14.31 % to 0.01 %, and five composition rules"
		+ "hold without counter-example while two fall. A closed additionalProperties makes any"
		+ "drift of the game show at once, at the cost of maintenance at the next property, and it"
		+ "is what surfaced the property missing from the schema and the type. dependentRequired is"
		+ "a draft 2019-09 keyword that Ajv 8 refuses in strict mode under the draft-07 meta-schema"
		+ "of the ten schemas; switching the ten schemas and the validator would be a task of its"
		+ "own"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-09, applied by pull request 48"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST48

DECISION FloatSerializationIsCheckedInInfrastructure
	SPEC "No domain rule reads the text of a save"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules"
	SPEC "The float suffix check lives in infrastructure, beside schema validation, keeps its"
		+ "regular expression on the save text and attaches the issue code itself, imported from"
		+ "application"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateFloatSerialization.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure"
	REJECTED "Keeping the rule in the domain and passing it parsed entries: after JSON.parse, 5.0"
		+ "and 5 are the same double, and it would check nothing"
	REJECTED "Moving the check to shared-save-processing, which does not know ValidationIssue and"
		+ "has a single caller"
	RATIONALE "The domain neither serializes nor parses the format, and serialization errors belong"
		+ "in infrastructure: a missing .0 is a writing defect, not a business rule violation."
		+ "Emitting the suffix and checking it are two distinct moments: emission stays field by"
		+ "field at serialization (@DECISION.TheFloatSuffixIsAppliedAtEmission)"
		REF @DECISION.TheFloatSuffixIsAppliedAtEmission
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-12, user ruling at the launch of part A of the core-mapping"
		+ "boundaries task, pull request 62"
