DECISION AMergeTakesExactlyTwoSavesPerFolder
	SPEC "An input subfolder is merged only when it holds exactly two save files; any other count"
		+ "sets it aside"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::MERGEABLE_SAVE_FILES_COUNT"
	SPEC "A folder set aside is named on the error output with the count that disqualified it"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::renderSkippedFolder(folder,"
			+ "saveFileNames.length)"
	SPEC "The public documentation says two saves, because the code changed"
		IMPL "README.md::exactly 2"
	REJECTED "Accumulating the saves of a folder holding more than two files"
	REJECTED "Setting a folder aside without naming it, as a single-file folder already was"
	RATIONALE "The UI already took two files, save A and save B, so the accumulation loop of the"
		+ "CLI made the two entry points of the same tool say two different things; the user ruled"
		+ "in review to stay at two saves at most per merge"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-09, review of pull request 42"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST42

DECISION APlayerIdentityIsCarriedByItsEntry
	SPEC "The host role is applied by the position of the entry in save A, never by identifier"
		+ "equality nor by name"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergePlayers.ts::hostPositionInSaveA"
	SPEC "Save B supplies the host only when save A holds no player entry"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergePlayers.ts::hostPositionInSaveA ==="
			+ "NO_HOST_POSITION"
	SPEC "A player identifier is never regenerated"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/resolveIdConflicts.ts::Players are left"
			+ "out"
	SPEC "Deduplication and the host role are decided in a single rule module"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergePlayers.ts"
	REJECTED "Designating the host by identifier equality"
	REJECTED "Designating the host by name equality"
	REJECTED "Making up a new identifier for the save B player whose identifier already appears in"
		+ "save A: the value would designate no real account"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST43
	RESTS_ON @RULE.APlayerIdentifierIsCarriedAsExactDecimalText
	ASSUMES @HYPOTHESIS.APlayerIdentifierIsASteamAccountReusedAcrossGames
	RATIONALE "The identifier is unique neither across two saves nor, formally, within one;"
		+ "renumbering changed the account an entry names for nothing, since no entry references it"
		+ "back. Computing the role after renumbering would make a role rule depend on an"
		+ "identifier rule that knows nothing of it, and split one game rule across two modules."
		+ "Comparing by name fails too: nothing guarantees names are unique within a save, and two"
		+ "namesakes would both come out as hosts. The fallback to save B is bounded to the only"
		+ "reachable case, validation refusing upstream a non-empty players section without a host."
		+ "Accepted consequence: two player entries can carry the same Steam account, a case the"
		+ "deduplication by name lets through by construction"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-07, pull request 39"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST39
	SOURCE "Extended in the review of pull request 41"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST41

DECISION AMergeThatWritesAFileIsASuccess
	SPEC "The use case validates its two inputs, merges, then validates what it produced, without a"
		+ "branch"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::const mergedSaveValidation ="
			+ "this.validator.validate(fileName, content);"
	SPEC "The errors of the merged file travel in a channel of their own, never folded into the"
		+ "per-input lists"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/responses/MergeSucceededResponse.ts::mergeErrors"
	SPEC "The warnings of the revalidation are not reported: a merge success carries the warnings"
		+ "of its two inputs only"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::saveAWarnings:"
			+ "validationA.warnings"
	SPEC "A merge that could not produce a result has a dedicated presenter outcome and a non-zero"
		+ "exit code"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/MergeResultPresenterPort.ts::presentMergedSaveUnusable"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::exitProcess(UNEXPECTED_ERROR_EXIT_CODE)"
	SPEC "In the CLI, the failure marker on a line marks an invalid merged save and does not make"
		+ "the exit code non-zero"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::renderMergedSaveIssues(folder,"
			+ "viewModel.mergeErrors)"
	REJECTED "Refusing to write a file the revalidation finds invalid"
	REJECTED "An option that skips the revalidation step"
	REJECTED "Reporting the warnings of the revalidation like those of the inputs"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RATIONALE "Refusing to write would tie the availability of the merge to the severity of the"
		+ "validator. Announcing that a save was created by an older game version, about a file the"
		+ "tool has just written, is nonsense: that vocabulary does not apply to an output. The"
		+ "measured cost of the revalidation is +25 % of a merge, the world objects section now"
		+ "going through ajv"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-07, delivered by pull request 59"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST59

DECISION NoMergeWarningChannelWithoutAProducer
	SPEC "The merge exposes no warning channel on its output while no merge rule produces a warning"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/MergeResultPresenterPort.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/responses/MergeSucceededResponse.ts"
	SPEC "The day a rule produces one, the channel is a single list about the output, under one"
		+ "name from the field of the port response to the ViewModel"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/responses/MergeSucceededResponse.ts"
	REJECTED "Opening the channel now, ahead of need"
	REJECTED "Folding the output warnings into the per-input lists"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RATIONALE "A channel without a producer is dead code, and the two candidates are not producers:"
		+ "an empty section is legitimate in a valid save, and an identifier collision is a fixed"
		+ "defect, not a feature to document. The name of the channel is the same end to end; its"
		+ "neighbours in the same interface already take that form, without a Messages suffix,"
		+ "because validation messages travel as a message and location pair, not as a string"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-10, pull request 54"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST54
	SOURCE "Name settled in the review of pull request 59"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST59

DECISION AMergeProducesAnOrdinarySave
	SPEC "resolveIdConflicts returns a SaveSections, entries of save A before those of save B,"
		+ "single-entry sections put in an array"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/resolveIdConflicts.ts"
	SPEC "One save parser, SaveSectionsParserPort, returns a SaveSections and its unreadable lines,"
		+ "without throwing, when loading as when merging"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveSectionsParserPort.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/SaveSectionsParserService.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/LoadAndValidateSaveFile.ts"
	SPEC "One serializer, SaveSectionsSerializerPort, writes a SaveSections and knows nothing of a"
		+ "merge nor of the origin of entries"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveSectionsSerializerPort.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/SaveSectionsSerializerService.ts"
	SPEC "The use case itself calls the merge and identifier resolution rules between the parser"
		+ "and the serializer"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::resolveIdConflicts(mergeSaveSections("
	SPEC "The unusable merge outcome keeps its trigger: an unreadable line reported by the parser,"
		+ "which walks the world objects section on reading"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::this.presenter.presentMergedSaveUnusable();"
	SPEC "No ViewModel nor controller carries ParsedSections, and ui-save-manager no longer depends"
		+ "on shared-save-processing"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/viewModels/LoadSaveFileViewModel.ts"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/package.json::ui-save-manager"
	SPEC "The merged file name is computed in the application layer by the pure function"
		+ "nameMergedFile, from a named object, not through a port"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/nameMergedFile.ts"
	SPEC "SaveSections, InventoryEntry and WorldObjectEntry are the save model of the domain and"
		+ "live in domain/save; no merge rule declares them"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/save"
	REJECTED "A serializer specific to the merge result, taking the sections by origin: a service"
		+ "for a single case, and a merge rule in infrastructure"
	REJECTED "A second read port beside SaveSectionsParserPort, one returning the wire tuple when"
		+ "loading and the other the save model when merging: two ports reading a save from its"
		+ "content"
	REJECTED "A port to name the merged file: a pure function is not an external capability"
		+ "(ARCH-CA-APP-3)"
	REJECTED "Leaving the save model under rules/merge: a parser and a serializer of an ordinary"
		+ "save do not take a merge model"
	REJECTED "A distinct assembly rule after resolveIdConflicts: a third domain call and an"
		+ "intermediate type for a projection the last consumer of the origin makes itself"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	RATIONALE "A serialization service specific to merge results has no reason to exist, nor has a"
		+ "second read port when loading already has one. MergedSaveSections existed only for"
		+ "identifier resolution, its last consumer, so resolution returns the save;"
		+ "MergedSaveSections and EntriesByOrigin stay internal to the merge, between"
		+ "mergeSaveSections and resolveIdConflicts, as the merge rules receive them (see"
		+ "@DECISION.MergeRulesReceiveTheDomainSaveModel). The A-then-B order on writing is a merge"
		+ "rule; it lived in the infrastructure serializer and returns to the domain"
		REF @DECISION.MergeRulesReceiveTheDomainSaveModel
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-12, review of pull request 62 by the user in two passes: a merge"
		+ "result is an ordinary save, and the existing parser is reused to read it"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST62

DECISION InputFolderScanRecognizesSavesWithHasJsonExtension
	SPEC "The scan of an input folder keeps a save file through hasJsonExtension, whatever the case"
		+ "of the extension"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::filter(hasJsonExtension)"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.spec.js"
	SPEC "cli-merge declares shared-save-processing as a production dependency"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/package.json::cli-merge"
	REJECTED "Keeping the case sensitivity and declaring it intended: it is intended nowhere else,"
		+ "and the folder is then reported as not holding two saves, a diagnosis that does not name"
		+ "the cause"
	REJECTED "Deferring the fix to a later task: it costs one line and one test case"
	RATIONALE "hasJsonExtension is the only module that knows what the json extension is, so isJson"
		+ "leaves initMergeCli, and a folder of two saves one of which carries .JSON is merged"
		+ "instead of being announced as holding one. The fix leaves core-mapping and changes what"
		+ "bun merge picks up, which the task under way excluded; the user widened the scope of the"
		+ "pull request to take it. cli-merge declared shared-save-processing in devDependencies;"
		+ "the module becomes production code of the package, so the dependency moves to"
		+ "dependencies, as the cli-* to shared-* matrix allows"
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-14, review of pull request 76"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST76

DECISION AnEmptyMetadataSectionIsRefusedByValidation
	SPEC "Validation refuses a save whose section 0 carries no entry, before any merge"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/save-file.schema.json::Section 0 — Player"
			+ "progression"
	SPEC "Reached by the merge anyway, an empty section 0 fails with a named error, never with a"
		+ "bare TypeError"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeGlobalMetadata.ts::openedInstanceSource"
	REJECTED "Restoring the ERROR_INVALID_INPUT_FORMAT verdict from before the refactor: it never"
		+ "refused the merge, it wrote a save whose section 0 carries that text, with exit code 0"
	REJECTED "Falling back from openedInstanceSource to DEFAULT_METADATA: the merge would produce a"
		+ "save from two invalid inputs, with an instance seed of zero, while what the user must"
		+ "see of a corrupted save is the refusal of validation"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FIX45
	RATIONALE "Measured on 2026-09-15: mergeGlobalMetadata([], []) throws TypeError, and bun merge"
		+ "on a folder of two saves with an empty section 0 prints « Error: undefined is not an"
		+ "object » then exits with 1 without writing a file. On origin/master the"
		+ "ERROR_INVALID_INPUT_FORMAT verdict did not refuse the merge: it was the return value of"
		+ "mergeSaves, hence the written content of section 0, with exit code 0, as merge.spec.js"
		+ "asserted verbatim. The branch therefore replaces a corrupted save written silently by a"
		+ "loud failure without writing; what remains to fix is the form of the failure, not its"
		+ "outcome. The ruling on error paths already carries the remedy: an error on an input file"
		+ "belongs to validation, and the same error reached further is a broken invariant that"
		+ "fails loudly (@DECISION.AnErrorsOriginDecidesItsPath)"
		REF @DECISION.AnErrorsOriginDecidesItsPath
	SOURCE "Review of pull request 15, measures of 2026-09-15"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST15

DECISION ThePrivateContextIgnoreRuleHasNoTrailingSlash
	SPEC "The public ignore rule targets .do-not-commit without a trailing slash nor a prefix, like"
		+ "input, so that it takes the link as it takes the directory, and carries the comment that"
		+ "says why"
		IMPL ".gitignore::.do-not-commit"
	REJECTED "Keeping the trailing slash and relying on vigilance at staging time"
	RATIONALE "It is exactly the defect already met on input/, widened to input by pull request 37;"
		+ "the link carries the absolute path of the user's private clone, and a commit would"
		+ "expose it in the public repository. Mounting the corpus makes the case common: linking"
		+ "the private clone in a worktree becomes a normal gesture. CFG-2 prescribes it word for"
		+ "word: no trailing slash when a symbolic link to the directory must be taken, and the"
		+ "comment that says why is part of the rule"
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-11 while mounting the awawa corpus"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION TestsOutsideAPackageRootLoadThePreloadThroughBunOptions
	SPEC "Tests run from a directory where Bun finds no bunfig.toml load the preload through"
		+ "BUN_OPTIONS pointing to it by absolute path, on the model of the IDE's Bun configuration"
		IMPL "README.md::BUN_OPTIONS=--preload=<absolute path>/testSetup.ts"
	SPEC "The isolation spec, run with the working directory to check, fails when the preload does"
		+ "not apply"
