DECISION TheByteOrderMarkIsNotPreserved
	SPEC "Both platform adapters strip the byte order mark on reading and write none, honouring the"
		+ "same read and write contract"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.fs.adapters.spec.js::When the file starts with a"
			+ "byte order mark"
	SPEC "A save prefixed with a byte order mark merges correctly in a real Node process, the"
		+ "content asserted and not only the exit code"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.node.spec.js::When an input save is prefixed with a"
			+ "byte order mark"
	REJECTED "Carrying the mark as domain metadata"
	RATIONALE "A round trip is therefore not byte-identical on a file carrying a mark. The game"
		+ "loads both forms, and the marks found in the reference saves come from an editor, not"
		+ "from the game: Custom-1.json carries one, Standard-1, 3 and 4 do not. Preserving the"
		+ "mark would mean carrying it as metadata through a domain that has no business knowing"
		+ "encodings, with merge inputs that may disagree and hence no defensible rule for the"
		+ "output"
	SOURCE "Private context file known-issues/merge/marque-d-ordre-des-octets-non-preservee.md, at"
		+ "tag pcst/before-awawa"
		REF @PROJECT.DNC
