DECISION AMergeIntroducesNoIdOverlapAbsentFromItsInputs
	SPEC "The rule of the shared numbering space states what the merge does not introduce, never"
		+ "the uniqueness of the union: the merge introduces no identifier overlap absent from its"
		+ "input saves"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/rules.awawa::the merge introduces into that space no"
			+ "duplicate the input saves did not already carry"
	REJECTED "Renumbering entries of save A to make the union unique"
	REJECTED "Letting the rule state the uniqueness of the union, which is false on real saves"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RESTS_ON @RULE.IdentifiersAreSharedByInventoriesAndWorldObjects
	RATIONALE "The input saves already carry the overlap, written by the game, and no merge can"
		+ "remove it. Measured on 2026-09-07 on the reference folders: Standard-3 has 721 values"
		+ "carried both by an inventory and a world object, Standard-4 549, Standard-1-unlocked-ivy"
		+ "203, Standard-1 171; both sections number in the same range 101 000 000 – 110 000 000"
		+ "and the game readily reuses a value of one in the other. Removing the overlap would"
		+ "require renumbering entries of save A, whose identifiers are authoritative and which the"
		+ "tool has no reason to touch. One overlap was introduced per folder before the fix of"
		+ "pull request 41, none after"
	SOURCE "Private context file"
		+ "known-issues/merge/recouvrement-d-identifiants-deja-present-dans-les-saves-d-entree.md,"
		+ "at tag pcst/before-awawa"
