DECISION NpmIsSupportedForUsersNotForTheProject
	SPEC "The workspace declares explicit version ranges rather than catalog references, and a"
		+ "shared version goes through a root override"
		IMPL "package.json::\"overrides\""
	SPEC "Bun's lockfile is the only lockfile of the project; npm's is ignored by git and never"
		+ "maintained"
		IMPL ".gitignore::package-lock.json"
	REJECTED "Keeping catalog references and giving up npm support"
	REJECTED "Maintaining a second lockfile"
	RATIONALE "npm rejects the catalog and workspace protocols so that an npm install passes for a"
		+ "user, and the dependency update tool does not resolve a catalog either: a dependency"
		+ "declared through a catalog is never bumped, with no pull request and no warning"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-07, pull request 34; blind spot of catalogs found on 2026-09-10"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST34

DECISION TypeCheckRunsPerPackageWithoutAnOrchestrator
	SPEC "Each package carries its TypeScript configuration and type-check script, and the root"
		+ "chains them through the workspace filter, without a monorepo orchestrator"
		IMPL "package.json::lint:types"
	SPEC "Only UI packages declare the browser libraries, so a browser global referenced from a"
		+ "core or cli package fails instead of resolving silently"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/tsconfig.json::\"dom\""
	SPEC "No root script names a path internal to a package: a package carrying two programs chains"
		+ "them itself"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/package.json::tsc --noEmit && tsc --noEmit --project e2e"
	REJECTED "A monorepo orchestrator"
	REJECTED "A root script naming a path internal to a package"
	RATIONALE "One configuration file and one script per package are enough, so the planning"
		+ "reservation against a monorepo orchestrator never had to be engaged. The two programs of"
		+ "one package carried the same script key, and merging the manifests had kept only one,"
		+ "silently"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-04, delivered by pull request 44"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST44

DECISION TheQualityGateRunsInTwoCiJobs
	SPEC "CI covers the ground of the quality audit in two jobs, one running the guards, the other"
		+ "the audit and the health report of the analysis tool, both rendered in the run summary,"
		+ "without running anything twice"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::guards:"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::fallow:"
	SPEC "The full audit command stays that of a working copy and is not plugged as is into a job"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml"
	REJECTED "Plugging the full audit command into a job"
	REJECTED "Keeping the analysis tool out of CI"
	REJECTED "Switching the scripts to a tracking reference and removing the analysis job, which"
		+ "fixed the symptom at the cost of the summary"
	RATIONALE "CI does not have to run the same command as the workstation, it has to cover the"
		+ "same ground. The audit scripts scope on a bare branch name, which a CI checkout does not"
		+ "resolve: measured, scoping by bare name errors where scoping by tracking reference"
		+ "passes. The action scopes on the base of the pull request, which is more accurate on a"
		+ "branch stack"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-09, pull request 45, second round"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST45

DECISION NodeFollowsReleasesWhileBunIsPinnedAndBumped
	SPEC "No workflow carries a literal Bun version: all read it from the manifest"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::bun-version-file: package.json"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/dependencies.yml::bun-version-file: package.json"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/ui-tests.yml::bun-version-file: package.json"
	SPEC "The Node version is an open range in the manifest"
		IMPL "package.json::\"engines\""
	SPEC "The root manifest declares bun in devDependencies at an exact version, the same version"
		+ "in packageManager, and the supported floor as an open range in engines.bun"
		IMPL "package.json::\"packageManager\""
		IMPL "package.json::\"bun\": \">=1.3.14\""
	REJECTED "Freezing Bun without a bump path, on the ground that it would be tooling and not a"
		+ "target runtime"
	REJECTED "Pinning Node like Bun: the open range is the coverage of the fallback path"
	REJECTED "Repeating the versions in the workflows instead of reading them from the manifest"
	REJECTED "Declaring bun as the range ^1.3.14: the range resolves the latest release at the"
		+ "first install and bumps the lock without going through Dependabot, as measured; an exact"
		+ "version is bumped by the bot just as well"
	REJECTED "Making engines.bun the field CI reads: an open range there resolves the latest"
		+ "release and kills the cache"
	REJECTED "A guard comparing packageManager with the declaration Dependabot bumps: it would fail"
		+ "on every pull request of the bot, which touches only one"
	REJECTED "An automation realigning packageManager by a commit pushed on the Dependabot branch:"
		+ "an unreviewed commit in place of a reviewed line"
	RATIONALE "Bun is the target runtime of the CLIs and Node the fallback path for whoever has not"
		+ "installed it, so following Bun releases tests the runtime the product promises first."
		+ "oven-sh/setup-bun reads packageManager first and engines.bun only as a fallback, and"
		+ "resolves a range to the latest satisfying release, so packageManager is the only field"
		+ "CI can read and it carries a concrete version, which also keeps an exact, stable cache"
		+ "key between two bumps. Dependabot never touched packageManager nor engines in the bun"
		+ "ecosystem: the lever is a dependency entry, and devDependencies is its true place, the"
		+ "package being repository tooling. No configuration makes a single field carry the"
		+ "version, so realigning packageManager is a gesture of the review of the Dependabot pull"
		+ "request, not a CI gate"
	SOURCE "Correction of 2026-09-16: the premise that Bun is build and test tooling, corrected by"
		+ "the user"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST90
	SOURCE "Blocking measured on pull requests 57 and 89: the first bumped bun, the second bumps"
		+ "only @types/bun"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST57
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST89

DECISION DependabotTracksTwoEcosystemsInWeeklyGroups
	SPEC "The configuration tracks two ecosystems from the root, the CI actions and the workspace"
		+ "dependencies, one group per ecosystem, weekly, with a pull request limit raised"
		+ "explicitly"
		IMPL ".github/dependabot.yml::open-pull-requests-limit: 10"
	SPEC "The package manager ecosystem only makes version updates; the vulnerability audit stays"
		+ "the safety net"
		IMPL ".github/dependabot.yml::package-ecosystem: \"bun\""
	SPEC "Pull requests opened by the bot are excluded from the automatic review"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml::github.actor != 'dependabot[bot]'"
	REJECTED "Leaving the pull request limit at its default value"
	REJECTED "Separating production and development in the package manager group"
	REJECTED "Keeping the automatic review on the bot's pull requests"
	RATIONALE "The default limit is five, and a queue truncated silently is refused. The production"
		+ "and development split in a group is not honoured by this ecosystem; the file carries the"
		+ "comment that says so, so that a reviewer does not restore an inert split. Bot pull"
		+ "requests receive a read-only token and no secret, so the review job would fail every"
		+ "time. Verified on the first real run: two pull requests opened within three minutes, and"
		+ "the actor guard works"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-10, pull request 53, verified on a real run"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST53

DECISION SharedSaveProcessingOwnsSectionParsingAndSerialization
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	SPEC "shared-save-processing exposes the parsing and the serialization of save sections"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/package.json::Save file wire format: types, parsing,"
			+ "serialization and schemas"
	REJECTED "Parse or serialize save sections in a package other than shared-save-processing"
	SOURCE "package rule recorded with the package entity"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION BothPlatformAdaptersHonourOneSharedContract
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_platforms
	SPEC "The Bun and Node adapters honour the same contract, verified by one spec shared by both"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.js::RuntimePlatform"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/shared-platforms/platform.fs.adapters.spec.js::FILE_ACCESS_ADAPTERS"
	REJECTED "One spec per adapter, each free to pin its own behaviour"
	SOURCE "package rule recorded with the package entity"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION CoreMappingExportsOnlyControllersAndViewModels
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "Only the controllers and the ViewModels are exported: no infrastructure module is"
		+ "reachable from outside the package"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/package.json::./controllers/*"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/package.json::./presentation/viewModels/*"
	REJECTED "Export infrastructure modules of core-mapping to its consumers"
	SOURCE "package rule recorded with the package entity"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION EachUseCaseResponseIsDeclaredInItsOwnFile
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "The Responses of the use cases are declared in application/responses, one interface per"
		+ "file"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/responses"
	REJECTED "Declare a Response beside the port it crosses"
	RATIONALE "The port is the boundary, not the payload that crosses it; application/requests"
		+ "already held the other half of the rule"
	SOURCE "T28"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST59

DECISION UiSaveManagerStaysOutsideTheFallowPerimeter
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	UNTIL "ui-save-manager is brought into the fallow quality perimeter"
	SPEC "ui-save-manager is outside the fallow quality perimeter"
