DECISION DissolvedPackagesAreNotRecreated
	DESC "util-parsing, util-messages and shared-mapping were dissolved into shared-save-processing"
		+ "and core-mapping; util-platforms was renamed shared-platforms"
	SPEC "No dissolved package is recreated, and no new util-* package is created except for a"
		+ "truly generic helper; file format helpers go into shared-save-processing"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::ont été dissous"
	REJECTED "Recreate a util-* package for a file format helper"
	RATIONALE "YAGNI: one package per family of helpers multiplies boundaries without separating"
		+ "responsibilities"
	SOURCE "private AGENTS.md, section « Organisation des packages », tag pcst/before-awawa"
		REF @PROJECT.DNC

DECISION MergeRulesReceiveTheDomainSaveModel
	DESC "the domain save model in domain/save is a record of named sections whose inventories and"
		+ "world objects carry their identifier lists as numbers, the other sections staying the"
		+ "wire DTOs documented as domain input; the merge rules receive it and return it"
		REF @DECISION.AMergeProducesAnOrdinarySave
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	SPEC "No domain type is named after an infrastructure operation, and no merge rule of the"
		+ "domain imports a section index or the parsed tuple type"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge"
	SPEC "Reading and writing an identifier list are declared in shared-save-processing, beside the"
		+ "DTO that declares the field, and called from the infrastructure mappers only"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/idList.js::parseIdList"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/idList.js::serializeIdList"
	REJECTED "Merge rules taking wire DTO strings, the comma being part of the documented format:"
		+ "the domain would parse a persistence encoding"
	REJECTED "Keep the Decoded* types and the eleven-slot tuple under new names: the name was only"
		+ "the symptom, the file layout inside the domain was the violation"
	REJECTED "A codec module in the core-mapping infrastructure: two infrastructure mappers needed"
		+ "it, and the knowledge of the field belongs to the package that declares it"
	RATIONALE "The previous form rejected a merge model while building half of one: three Decoded*"
		+ "types derived from the wire DTOs by Omit, and an eleven-slot tuple copying the file"
		+ "layout, reserved slot included, indexed from the domain by a shared-save-processing"
		+ "constant. A field encoding belongs to the format: the domain receives the field in its"
		+ "business form, and the package that declares the DTO knows what the string holds."
		+ "Reading in shared-save-processing was refused only while the domain would call it; with"
		+ "the model, only the infrastructure does"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-12, architecture review of the pull request by the user"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST62

DECISION WireAbbreviationsStayInSharedSaveProcessing
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "Wire format abbreviations are tolerated only in the shared-save-processing records and"
		+ "are translated into business language at the domain boundary"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/SaveSectionsParserService.ts"
	SPEC "The tolerance rests on the package description, not on a header comment in each file"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/package.json::Save file wire format"
	REJECTED "Tolerate wire abbreviations beyond this package"
	REJECTED "A header comment in each DTO file"
	RATIONALE "A comment per file says nothing the interface does not say, and it names a section"
		+ "by its index, a number no test holds and which becomes false the day an index moves"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-03, question Q8"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61
	SOURCE "header comments removed in the review of T36"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST55

DECISION CreateSaveRecordsIsTheOnlySourceOfRecordBuilders
	DESC "the two renderings, save string and already parsed sections, consume the record builders"
		+ "and are never their source"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST43
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST44
	SPEC "The save record builders are declared once, in the shared-save-processing testing"
		+ "directory, and imported one by one, without a barrel or a re-export for a historical"
		+ "caller"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/testing/createSaveRecords.js::createPlayer"
	SPEC "Every wire format record declared in the arrange phase of a spec goes through its"
		+ "builder, including when only a core package consumes it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/testing/createSaveRecords.js"
	REJECTED "Generate the fixtures from the JSON schemas"
	REJECTED "A barrel on the testing directory: it would recreate exactly the coupling removed"
	REJECTED "Convert the expected values too, which would make them recomputed"
	RATIONALE "The builders describe the wire format, not the domain. The rule stops at three"
		+ "boundaries: an expected value stays literal, domain types are not save records, and the"
		+ "serializer spec keeps its literals because each expectation there is the exact JSON of"
		+ "its field set. Generating from the JSON schemas would produce data nobody reads: a"
		+ "literal expectation reads, a generated value does not; one builder per type is the"
		+ "accepted cost"
	SOURCE "T21"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST35
	SOURCE "sweep rule extended in the review of T19"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST46

DECISION ASectionIndexIsNeverHardCoded
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST44
	SPEC "Section indexes, including those of the legacy format and the reserved part, are declared"
		+ "once and read from their module"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/sectionIndexes.js::PLAYERS_SECTION_INDEX"
	SPEC "No core-mapping spec hard-codes a section index, holey destructuring included; the number"
		+ "in an expected message stays literal"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.spec.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/LoadSaveFilePresenter.spec.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/MergeResultPresenter.spec.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/SaveFileValidationPresenter.spec.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatValidationError.spec.ts"
	REJECTED "Tolerate a literal index in a spec"
	REJECTED "Compose the expected message from the index module, which would make it recomputed"
	RATIONALE "User ruling, given twice on the same pull request. Part counts stay numbers: they"
		+ "are expectations, not accesses. The same boundary splits a location test in two: the"
		+ "input section: 2 is an access and is read from the module; the expectation Players"
		+ "(section 2), entry 3 is the sentence the formatter must render, and reading it from the"
		+ "module would make the expectation compute what it is meant to pin"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-09, review of T19 and T26"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61
	SOURCE "T44, boundary of the expectation settled at implementation"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST82

DECISION ACrossPackageJsdocTypeImportIsWrittenAsTypedef
	UNTIL "fallow follows the @import tag"
	SPEC "A JSDoc type import crossing a package boundary is written as a typedef carrying the"
		+ "import, the @import tag staying allowed inside a package; the only case carries the"
		+ "comment that keeps it from being normalised"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.js::@typedef"
			+ "{import('util-types/platform').RuntimePlatform} RuntimePlatform"
	REJECTED "Exclude the package from the dependency audit"
	REJECTED "Let the @import tag cross a package boundary"
	RATIONALE "The quality audit tool follows type imports written as calls in annotations, and the"
		+ "TypeScript 5.5 @import tag is invisible to it: the declared dependency is then reported"
		+ "as unused. The tool's dependency exclusion entry is no answer to a localised false"
		+ "positive: it disables both unused and undeclared dependency detection, for the whole"
		+ "repository and with no end date"
	SOURCE "T17"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST44

DECISION AnUnknownCliFlagIsAUsageError
	SPEC "Both CLIs name on standard error each dash-prefixed argument that designates none of"
		+ "their flags, print a usage line and exit with an error before reading anything"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/cliArguments.js::findUnknownArguments"
	SPEC "Flag parsing and unknown argument detection are shared by both CLIs, without creating a"
		+ "package; only dash-prefixed arguments are examined, the argument vector returned by the"
		+ "platform also carrying the interpreter and the script"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/cliArguments.js::readFlagValue"
	SPEC "The usage banner names the documented command in its Bun form under both runtimes"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/cliArguments.js"
	REJECTED "Warn without changing the exit code"
	REJECTED "Slice the argument vector to catch positionals, which would move the platform"
		+ "contract"
	REJECTED "Make the banner depend on the runtime"
	RATIONALE "A misspelt flag silently ignored makes the tool work on the default directories, and"
		+ "the result is indistinguishable from a success. Bun is the main maintained tool; the"
		+ "Node commands exist only for an accepted user-side compatibility, so the banner need not"
		+ "be runtime-aware"
	SOURCE "T34, banner settled in review"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST60

DECISION SectionControllersReceiveTheValidatedText
	DESC "the section controllers thus align on the merge controller, which already takes text, and"
		+ "the UI no longer knows any representation of the sections"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "No section controller imports SaveSectionsReaderService or receives a SaveSections: each"
		+ "takes the save text and gets its reader from the composition root, which parses the text"
		+ "with the existing parser and discards unreadable lines"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/controllers"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/composition/compositionRoot.ts::createSaveSectionsReader"
	SPEC "The load ViewModel no longer carries sections"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/viewModels/LoadSaveFileViewModel.ts"
	SPEC "The UI keeps the validated text in a signal set when the load status is valid, and feeds"
		+ "the section resources from it"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/lib/useLoadSaveFile.ts"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/lib/useSectionViewModels.ts"
	REJECTED "An opaque identifier of the loaded save carried by the ViewModel, with a registry in"
		+ "core-mapping keeping the parsed sections: state in a stateless package, and the merge"
		+ "controller would stay on another contract"
	RATIONALE "Unreadable lines are discarded without loss: the load, sole presenter of these"
		+ "errors, has already rendered them, and a second parse of the same text is deterministic."
		+ "Measured on 2026-09-13 under Bun on input/Test/Standard-3.json, 2.02 MB: 11.5 ms per"
		+ "parse on average over 20 runs, about 60 ms for the five sections of a load; each section"
		+ "carries its own loading state, so the overhead stays invisible"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-13, user ruling at the launch of T37 part B"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST65

DECISION BehaviourMovesOntoTheEntityAndTheRuleAsksIt
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "The fuse count of an optimizer filters the world objects of the whole save by name and by"
		+ "inventory.contains, instead of walking the inventory identifier list through a table of"
		+ "world objects indexed by identifier"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/InventoryEntity.ts"
	SPEC "No distance function remains in domain/rules: the geometry of placed objects lives on"
		+ "PlacedWorldObjectEntity and the optimizer is asked"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/PlacedWorldObjectEntity.ts::boostedProducersAmong"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts"
	SPEC "computeTerraformationSummary is removed: summarize returns the whole"
		+ "TerraformationLevelSummaryValueObject, which declares its ten fields instead of"
		+ "extending the entity, and the use case calls level.summarize() and composes nothing"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/TerraformationLevelEntity.ts::summarize()"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/LoadTerraformationLevelsSection.ts::level.summarize()"
	REJECTED "A contains taking a WorldObjectEntity rather than an identifier: the inventory would"
		+ "depend on another entity for a membership question"
	RATIONALE "contains is the behaviour the task moves onto InventoryEntity; keeping the original"
		+ "walk would have left the worldObjectIds getter carrying the rule and contains without a"
		+ "caller. Both forms count the same thing while world object identifiers are unique in a"
		+ "save: the original form already deduplicated through a Map indexed by identifier, so it"
		+ "made the same assumption without saying so; a duplicated identifier would now count once"
		+ "per world object instead of once per inventory entry, and no save read shows the case."
		+ "distanceTo comes with isWithinRadius because the selection of boosted producers sorts by"
		+ "distance before cutting at the optimizer capacity. An interface extending a class"
		+ "inherits its private fields and methods, so the value object would have carried"
		+ "summarize; declaring the ten fields and returning the whole value object removes the"
		+ "last two entity spreads, in the factory and in the use case"
	SOURCE "T15, migration of behaviour onto the entities"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST72

DECISION AnEntityReturnsACopyOfItsInternalArray
	DESC "a domain entity exposes no mutator: any future mutation goes through an entity method"
		+ "that rebuilds the state"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "InventoryEntity.worldObjectIds, PlayerEntity.inventory, PlayerEntity.equipment and"
		+ "PlacedWorldObjectEntity.position return a copy: mutating the returned array changes"
		+ "neither what the entity exposes next nor what contains answers"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/InventoryEntity.ts::[...this._worldObjectIds]"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/PlayerEntity.ts::[...this._inventory]"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/PlayerEntity.ts::[...this._equipment]"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/PlacedWorldObjectEntity.ts::[...this._position]"
	REJECTED "Return the array as is, protected by the readonly type alone"
	REJECTED "Freeze the array with Object.freeze in the constructor: the mutation would fail"
		+ "silently outside strict mode, and the error would stay unreadable"
	RATIONALE "The readonly type alone is undone by an assertion, and the invariant the constructor"
		+ "validated falls without notice; the copy is the only guard the compiler cannot bypass."
		+ "The feared cost does not exist: the hot path is InventoryEntity.contains, which reads"
		+ "the private field, and the only accessor callers are the sections reader, twice per"
		+ "player, and the players presenter, once per player"
	SOURCE "review of the pull request by the repository owner, T15"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST72

DECISION APlacedWorldObjectIsAWorldObject
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "PlacedWorldObjectEntity extends WorldObjectEntity: a placed object is a world object that"
		+ "also carries a position, a planet and an inventory"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/PlacedWorldObjectEntity.ts::export class"
			+ "PlacedWorldObjectEntity extends WorldObjectEntity"
	SPEC "No conversion helper from placed object to world object remains in src/testing: a spec"
		+ "needing the whole save list puts the built entities in it directly"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/testing"
	REJECTED "Keep two independent classes and the test helper: the helper built a second entity"
		+ "from the identity of a first, work that only the nominal incompatibility made necessary"
	RATIONALE "Two classes were imposed only by the commit order of T15, when WorldObjectEntity was"
		+ "converted while PlacedWorldObjectEntity was still an interface; all five entities are"
		+ "now converted. Liskov substitution holds: every caller expecting a world object identity"
		+ "accepts a placed object, and no signature needs the position. Production is unchanged:"
		+ "the sections reader already builds the whole save list and the placed objects in two"
		+ "separate passes, unplaced objects staying WorldObjectEntity"
	SOURCE "review of the pull request by the repository owner, T15"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST72

DECISION EnergyRulesAskThePlacedObjectNotTheTables
	DESC "energyOptimizerConfig lives in domain, not domain/rules: it is configuration read by the"
		+ "entities, not a rule"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "A placed object tells its production level, its consumption level and whether it is an"
		+ "optimizer; an optimizer chooses the producers it boosts itself, distanceTo and"
		+ "isWithinRadius being private"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/PlacedWorldObjectEntity.ts::boostedProducersAmong"
	SPEC "A world object tells whether it is an energy fuse"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/entities/WorldObjectEntity.ts::isEnergyFuse"
	SPEC "No energy rule indexes energyProductionLevelsByWorldObjectName,"
		+ "energyConsumptionLevelsByWorldObjectName or OPTIMIZER_CONFIG_BY_NAME by an entity name,"
		+ "except computeEnergyBreakdown, which receives its table as a parameter"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts"
	REJECTED "Delete each rule and call the entity method at the call site: a sum or a join over a"
		+ "collection belongs to no single entity"
	REJECTED "Move validateUniqueHost and resolvePlanetName: the first takes the raw Player of"
		+ "shared-save-processing, not PlayerEntity, and the second concerns no entity"
	RATIONALE "What follows from the name of a world object alone is the state of that object: a"
		+ "rule indexing a table by entity.name is feature envy, and the class conversion of T15"
		+ "makes the fix possible, as the behaviour migration already did. computeEnergyBreakdown"
		+ "does not move: it is parameterised by the table it receives and serves twice, production"
		+ "and consumption, and making it entity-dependent would force its specs to cite real game"
		+ "values instead of a test table. Grouping radius, range and capacity in"
		+ "boostedProducersAmong leaves the joining of inventories to optimizers to count fuses as"
		+ "the one thing outside the entity"
		REF @DECISION.BehaviourMovesOntoTheEntityAndTheRuleAsksIt
	SOURCE "review of the pull request by the repository owner, T15"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST72

DECISION APlanetEnergyGridIsAnAggregate
	DESC "optimizer boosts and fuse counts are computed once in the constructor and read again by"
		+ "each accessor"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "PlanetEnergyGrid, built with the PlanetWorldObjectsValueObject of the planet, the world"
		+ "objects of the whole save and the inventories, returns through levels() the complete"
		+ "PlanetEnergyLevelsValueObject built by its factory and carrying planetId"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts::levels():"
			+ "PlanetEnergyLevelsValueObject"
	SPEC "None of the six energy rules turned into private methods of the grid remains in"
		+ "domain/rules, the cases they pinned being re-anchored on levels()"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.spec.ts"
	SPEC "LoadEnergyLevelsSection builds one grid per planet, collects its levels and copies no"
		+ "field"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/LoadEnergyLevelsSection.ts"
	REJECTED "Make computePlanetEnergyLevels take the PlanetWorldObjectsValueObject and return the"
		+ "complete value object: the unvalidated literal went away, but the triple still crossed"
		+ "five signatures and the triple computation stayed"
	REJECTED "Have the presentation assemble the value object: the PresenterPort would stop"
		+ "receiving a domain value"
	REJECTED "Build the value objects field by field in the use case: the rule would still return a"
		+ "literal the factory does not validate"
	RATIONALE "The five energy rules all took the same triple allWorldObjects,"
		+ "positionedWorldObjectsOnPlanet, inventories: a triple crossing five signatures intact is"
		+ "an unnamed object. The cost was not only style: computeOptimizerBoosts ran three times"
		+ "per planet, each run redoing the fuse scan and the boosted producer selection. This is"
		+ "not the option the energy rules decision refuses, which is making a sum or a join over a"
		+ "collection a method of a single entity: the object to create is an aggregate, the grid"
		+ "of the planet, and computeEnergyBreakdown stays a rule parameterised by its table. The"
		+ "grid is a sixth domain object beyond the five entities of T15, an extension decided by"
		+ "the repository owner in the pull request. The twenty-two cases of the six deleted specs"
		+ "are re-anchored on levels() without weakening"
		REF @DECISION.EnergyRulesAskThePlacedObjectNotTheTables
	SOURCE "ruling of the repository owner in review, deliberate extension of T15"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST72

DECISION APresenterReceivesAValueObjectNeverAnEntity
	DESC "the infrastructure keeps the right to build entities and SaveSectionsReaderPort still"
		+ "carries them: only the presentation boundary is closed"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "No PresenterPort declares a domain entity: PlayersPresenterPort carries"
		+ "PlayerSummaryValueObject"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/PlayersPresenterPort.ts::PlayerSummaryValueObject"
	SPEC "No presentation file imports domain/entities"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/PlayersPresenter.ts"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-presentation-entities.ts"
		ENFORCED_BY "package.json::check:presentation"
	SPEC "The use case does the projection: LoadPlayersSection builds PlayerSummaryValueObject from"
		+ "the entity through its factory"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/LoadPlayersSection.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/valueObjects/PlayerSummaryValueObject.ts"
	REJECTED "The strict reading, an entity never travels outside domain and application: it would"
		+ "have taken SaveSectionsReaderService, its spec and the fake reader, and forced"
		+ "validation out of the constructor where T15 had just put it; its real gain is the"
		+ "question of where a save is validated, which deserves a task of its own"
	REJECTED "A projection method on PlayerEntity by symmetry with level.summarize(): summarize"
		+ "computes biomass and index while a player projection computes nothing, so summarize"
		+ "stays reserved for entities that compute and the factory is called from the use case"
		REF @DECISION.BehaviourMovesOntoTheEntityAndTheRuleAsksIt
	RATIONALE "An entity carries behaviour: a presenter holding one decides when a domain"
		+ "computation runs, and PlayerEntity has been a class since T15. The shape of an entity"
		+ "follows the save format and the domain invariants, not what is displayed. Since the"
		+ "accessors copy, PlayersPresenter paid two allocations per player reading inventory and"
		+ "equipment, while a value object is already flat. The rule was a convention nothing broke"
		+ "in red: check:dependencies reasons on package prefixes, not internal directories, so a"
		+ "guard script follows the form of the others. The price is lasting: every future section"
		+ "that displays an entity pays a value object and a projection step"
		REF @DECISION.AnEntityReturnsACopyOfItsInternalArray
	SOURCE "ruling of the repository owner in review, restricted reading, work done in the pull"
		+ "request rather than in T38"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST72

DECISION AReaderPortIsNamedForWhatItReads
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SPEC "The reader port names its methods for what they return, getGlobalProgression returning a"
		+ "GlobalProgressionValueObject, and its holders for what it is: a parameter or variable"
		+ "holding a SaveSectionsReaderPort is named saveSectionsReader, and its test double"
		+ "FakeSaveSectionsReaderService"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/ports/SaveSectionsReaderPort.ts::getGlobalProgression"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/LoadGlobalProgressionSection.ts::saveSectionsReader"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/testing/FakeSaveSectionsReaderService.ts"
	REJECTED "Have the port return the raw metadata and build the value object in the use case: the"
		+ "other five methods return a domain type, and this one would become the only one"
		+ "returning a save format record"
	REJECTED "Keep the method name and rename only the parameters: the gap the review raised is the"
		+ "name, and half a fix leaves it whole"
	RATIONALE "The six methods of the port return an entity or a value object since T15: the only"
		+ "gap left was between the method name and what it returns. Five use cases called parser"
		+ "the port that reads, whereas the parser is SaveSectionsParserPort, which takes save text"
		+ "and returns sections, and both ports live in the same directory"
		REF @DECISION.APresenterReceivesAValueObjectNeverAnEntity
	SOURCE "T38, reading of a SPEC line of the review of 2026-09-07"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST76

DECISION AColumnShapeIsDerivedFromTheTableViewModel
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "The shape of a table column is declared once, in the core-mapping table ViewModel, and"
		+ "the UI derives it from that ViewModel instead of declaring it again"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/viewModels/TableViewModel.ts::ColumnViewModel"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/structure/FieldsGroup.tsx::export type"
			+ "ColumnViewModel = TableViewModel['columns'][number];"
	REJECTED "Export ColumnViewModel from core-mapping and import it in the UI: the fix would leave"
		+ "the package the task anchors for a package another branch of the same wave rewrote, for"
		+ "a line the derivation gets without touching it"
	REJECTED "Keep both shapes and rely on structural compatibility"
	RATIONALE "The UI carried a Column type structurally identical to ColumnViewModel: two shapes"
		+ "nothing linked, either of which could drift unnoticed, TypeScript structural"
		+ "compatibility accepting one for the other"
	SOURCE "T32"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST71

DECISION SolidPropsAreReadThroughPropsNeverDestructured
	DESC "the rule targets the signature of a component, not the parameter of a callback:"
		+ "destructuring the item of a For has no effect on reactivity"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "No UI component destructures its props in its signature, even when a prop looks fixed"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/entry-server.tsx"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-solid-idioms.ts"
	REJECTED "Destructure when the prop looks fixed: the signature does not say what the parent"
		+ "will do on the next call"
	REJECTED "Get locals through splitProps or mergeProps: these primitives return props objects,"
		+ "not values"
	RATIONALE "Measured on 2026-09-14 with the repository's solid-js 1.9.14: a component called"
		+ "with the getter props object the compiler emits renders « save A » then « save A » again"
		+ "once the parent passes « save B », where the same component reading props.title renders"
		+ "« save A » then « save B »; the component function runs once, so destructuring reads"
		+ "every getter once and for all. Nothing in the signature tells a prop that never changes"
		+ "from one that will: the parent decides, later, without touching the component, so the"
		+ "rule is absolute or does not hold. The loss of reactivity is invisible to the build, the"
		+ "type-check and the scenarios; the eight sites fixed by T32 were all masked by an unmount"
		+ "and remount of the caller, which makes the defect latent, not absent"
	SOURCE "ruling in review, T32"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST71

DECISION AMessageVariantIsAFunctionNotTwinStrings
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "Two labels differing by one word are produced by a message function taking that word, the"
		+ "shared sentence being written once in the messages directory"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/appMessages.js"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/validationMessages.js"
	SPEC "Exported constants stay complete strings: the caller chooses a constant and assembles no"
		+ "sentence"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/appMessages.js"
	REJECTED "A placeholder notation in the string, {replace} or equivalent, with its formatting"
		+ "function: a template engine for two messages, where a function gives the same service"
		+ "and is checked by the compiler"
	REJECTED "Assemble the sentence in the JSX around a ternary: the user-facing sentence leaves"
		+ "the messages directory"
	RATIONALE "Written side by side, two twin sentences get changed one without the other and"
		+ "nothing signals it; the repository already parameterises a message by a function,"
		+ "resolvePlayersSectionUnknownItemLabel, so the form exists and need not be invented"
	SOURCE "ruling in review, T32"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST71

DECISION ADecorativeCharacterIsRenderedByIcon
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "A purely decorative character is rendered by the Icon component, which hides it from"
		+ "screen readers, and is not glued to the label in the message string: the accessible name"
		+ "of the 404 back link is the label alone"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/routes/[...404].tsx::<Icon"
			+ "content={notFoundRouteBackHomeIcon}/>"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/Icon.tsx"
	SPEC "The repository vocabulary is the icon, whatever the shape of the character: no component"
		+ "or message name carries the word Emoji"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/appMessages.js"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/HomeDisclaimer.tsx"
	REJECTED "An aria-label on the link: it duplicates the label, so it drifts"
	REJECTED "Keep the word Emoji for the component and speak of icon in the messages: two words"
		+ "for one role, and the choice comes back with each new character"
	RATIONALE "Glued to the label, the arrow of « ← Back home » enters the accessible name of the"
		+ "link and is announced before the text, teaching nothing. The mechanism already existed"
		+ "in the UI and served only one decorative character out of three. Emoji names a family of"
		+ "characters, not the rendered role: the back arrow is not one and goes through the same"
		+ "component, so the name covering both is icon"
	SOURCE "review of the pull request by the repository owner, T32, vocabulary corrected at the"
		+ "next review round"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST71

DECISION AGuardRefusesTheTwoLineReadableSolidIdioms
	DESC "the two other idiom criteria of T32, a map rendering JSX and a user string outside the"
		+ "messages directory, require reading the JSX and stay with review"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "The check:idioms guard refuses, in the tsx files of the packages, a props object"
		+ "destructured in a component signature and a non-null assertion on an accessor call"
		IMPL "scripts/check-solid-idioms.ts"
	SPEC "The accepted limit is pinned by a test that names it: an anonymous arrow destructuring"
		+ "the props of a component slot, the document shell of entry-server, cannot be told from a"
		+ "callback line by line and escapes the guard"
		IMPL "scripts/check-solid-idioms.spec.ts"
	SPEC "The guard runs alone and grouped behind the guards command"
		IMPL "package.json::bun scripts/check-solid-idioms.ts"
		IMPL "package.json::bun run check:idioms"
	SPEC "The guard and its spec are declared as entry points of the quality audit"
		IMPL "fallow.toml::scripts/check-solid-idioms.ts"
		IMPL "fallow.toml::scripts/check-solid-idioms.spec.ts"
	REJECTED "A configured linter instead of a dedicated script: already ruled out for the existing"
		+ "guards, and the reason has not changed"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	REJECTED "Cover all four criteria: the other two require reading the JSX, not lines"
	REJECTED "Run the guard on the whole repository rather than the tsx files: a destructured"
		+ "parameter object is the form STD-6 recommends everywhere else"
	RATIONALE "Replayed on the whole base tree of the branch, the guard reports twenty lines: seven"
		+ "destructured signatures, the five section components, FieldsGroupGrid and FieldsGroup,"
		+ "and the thirteen non-null assertions of MergeResultSection, exactly what T32 fixed; on"
		+ "the same tree it reports nothing for the document shell of entry-server, which T32 fixed"
		+ "too, which is the limit, measured on the same perimeter. It follows the form of the"
		+ "existing guards: no git history read, an answer in a fraction of a second, runnable"
		+ "alone and grouped, walk and report taken from the shared module. The targeted pattern is"
		+ "measured, not stylistic, which justifies a guard over a review habit"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
		REF @DECISION.SolidPropsAreReadThroughPropsNeverDestructured
	SOURCE "ruling in review, T32"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST71

DECISION TheCorpusLivesInThePublicRepository
	SPEC "The corpus is a set of files versioned in the public repository, under docs"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::La spécification du projet est le corpus awawa"
	SPEC "The workspace root is the root of the public repository, so awawa always runs from a"
		+ "worktree of that repository with . as root"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::La racine de workspace"
	REJECTED "Waiting for the awawa experiment to be confirmed: the fallback rests on a tag, not on"
		+ "where the corpus lives"
	REJECTED "Splitting the corpus into several files in the same move: the move is verified alone,"
		+ "and the split would be redone against a corpus that has moved"
	RATIONALE "Mounting the corpus by a link kept it outside the public repository and cost three"
		+ "things: a gitignore rule to maintain, a frozen clone per worktree in which a cited"
		+ "decision could be wrong without any sign, and a ruling kept apart from the code it"
		+ "governs, hence invisible in review; in the branch, a decision enters the pull request"
		+ "that implements it and follows the rebases of the stack"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-12"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION ThreeFilesAreChangedOnMasterFirst
	SPEC "dependabot.yml and the two claude workflows are changed on master first, and the task"
		+ "base receives them at its next rebase"
		IMPL ".github/dependabot.yml"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/claude.yml"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml"
	REJECTED "Treating these three files like the rest of the repository, changed from the task"
		+ "base"
	RATIONALE "dependabot.yml is only read on the default branch; claude-code-action validates both"
		+ "workflows against their copy on that same branch, and a differing content makes the"
		+ "action exit with a warning: the job is green and the review silently dead"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-10"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION NoRealPlayerNameInPublicContent
	SPEC "No real player name appears in public content: pull request title and body, review"
		+ "comments, code, tests, public fixtures, docs, README, commit messages"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::## Anonymisation des noms de joueurs"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Aucun nom réel"
	SPEC "Only these pseudonyms are allowed in public: Salengor, Chileny, Sovagoz, Nikowa, Sakia,"
		+ "Anya"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Seuls ces pseudonymes sont autorisés en public"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/baseline_valid.json::Nikowa"
	SPEC "The private repository keeps the real names as the source of truth, and the substitution"
		+ "happens when content goes public"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::c'est au moment de sortir en public qu'il faut substituer"
	SPEC "No mapping between a pseudonym and a real name is kept anywhere, since it would only"
		+ "serve to undo the anonymisation"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Aucune correspondance entre un pseudonyme et un nom réel"
	REJECTED "Rewriting the git history already pushed: the cost is out of proportion, and the"
		+ "compliance branch will likely be squashed at its merge"
	RATIONALE "The private saves carry the real names of players who did not consent to their"
		+ "publication; the rule stays written in full in AGENTS.md because forgetting it publishes"
		+ "personal data, the costliest mistake to reverse"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-10, PR #49"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST49

DECISION SteamIdentifiersAreAnonymisedLikeNames
	SPEC "Public content carries a synthetic identifier of the 765611900000000xx family, never the"
		+ "identifier of a real account"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::765611900000000xx"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/baseline_valid.json::76561190000000001"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/serializeSave.spec.js::76561190000000001"
	SPEC "The pattern pair replaces any mapping: 76561198… is a real identifier, 765611900000000xx"
		+ "a synthetic one"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::est un identifiant réel"
	SPEC "A demonstration identifier stays a true rounding pair: its exact text is not"
		+ "representable as a double and its printed value differs"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::doit rester un couple d'arrondi vrai"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/serializeSave.spec.js::When a save holding an int64"
			+ "player identifier is read back"
	REJECTED "Publishing the real identifiers on the ground that they carry no name"
	REJECTED "Taking any synthetic identifier: it would no longer demonstrate the rounding"
	RATIONALE "An account identifier designates a person as surely as a name"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-10"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION ThePrivateContextHoldsOnlySavesAndPlans
	SPEC "The private repository holds only the reference saves, the plans and resources.md: no"
		+ "instructions, no specification, no AGENTS.md"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::ne porte plus que ce qui ne peut pas être public"
	SPEC "The private clone is refreshed before reading a save or a plan, no longer before citing a"
		+ "decision or choosing a task number"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::private:sync"
	SPEC "The synchronisation is a repository script, called by the dependency install and runnable"
		+ "alone"
		IMPL "scripts/sync-private-context.sh"
		IMPL "package.json::private:sync"
		IMPL "package.json::postinstall"
	REJECTED "Deleting the private repository: the saves carry the real names of the players and"
		+ "weigh eight megabytes"
	REJECTED "Keeping the synchronisation at the start of a session: it no longer conditions"
		+ "anything a session reads to start"
	RATIONALE "The specification, the decisions and the task numbers are in the public repository:"
		+ "what a stale clone made wrong without a sign is no longer read there"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-12"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION NameMergedFileEscapesControlCharacters
	SPEC "nameMergedFile.ts writes its control-character class as escape sequences, never as raw"
		+ "bytes"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/nameMergedFile.ts::function sanitizeFileName"
	REJECTED "Promoting escape sequences over raw control bytes to a general rule, STD-8 in"
		+ "~/.ai/instructions/standards/coding.md: the case is marginal"
	REJECTED "Keeping it as a project rule in AGENTS.md: same reason, and nothing in the incident"
		+ "is specific to this repository"
	RATIONALE "A rule is worth the frequency of what it prevents; a raw control byte in a character"
		+ "class happened once, git made it visible through the binary diff, and the review fixed"
		+ "it in the commit that revealed it"
	SOURCE "user ruling of 2026-09-12, at the merge of PR #62"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST62

DECISION AUsageReportIsCommittedInTheTaskPullRequest
	SPEC "A task pull request gets one usage report file in"
		+ "docs/awawa-usage-reports/pull-requests/, following the template, committed on its branch"
		+ "before the merge once the review is addressed and the pull request flagged ready; a"
		+ "follow-up pull request gets none"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/_template.md"
	SPEC "The report is written by an independent agent through /awawa-usage-report: a fresh"
		+ "session with no memory of the work judged, never a fork, never the agent that"
		+ "implemented or reviewed"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/_template.md::never by a session that took"
	SPEC "The report names its author, the models of the sessions under review and the sessions"
		+ "measured"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/_template.md::Author of this report"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/_template.md::Sessions measured"
	SPEC "The file is named docs/awawa-usage-reports/pull-requests/<date>-pr-<N>.md, the date being"
		+ "that of the report"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/_template.md::-pr-<N>.md"
	SPEC "The template is the only home of the report shape: our verdict and the tool's, each by"
		+ "what went well, what went wrong and the remediations, then the recurring points with"
		+ "their occurrence counts, and the measures from the transcripts in an appendix"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/_template.md::## Verdict in two lines"
	SPEC "The report measures the ruling, the implementation and the review of the pull request,"
		+ "and cites entities without copying any"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/_template.md::Entities are cited by name and never"
	REJECTED "A separate report pull request: one more pull request to merge per task, as the chain"
		+ "#65, #67, #68, #69 showed"
	REJECTED "A report written after the merge: it would measure sessions that only recorded what"
		+ "the task pull request left out"
	REJECTED "A report written by the session that implements or the one that reviews: it grades"
		+ "its own work"
	REJECTED "A report on every merged pull request: the chain never closes"
	REJECTED "A report per session: only the whole pull request sees the complete course"
	REJECTED "The measures in the corpus: they are facts about the instrument, not about the"
		+ "project"
	RATIONALE "One pull request per task carries the code, the rulings and the report, and the"
		+ "merge brings them into the base at once with nothing running afterwards; the first usage"
		+ "report, written by the session at fault, held no measure and two overstated claims,"
		+ "found by an independent review"
		REF @PROCESS.EverythingLandsInTheTaskPullRequest
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-12, review of the first usage report"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST63
	SOURCE "user ruling of 2026-09-13 on PR #69, delivered by PR #70"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST69
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST70

DECISION AgentsMdNamesOneModelEntityPerType
	SPEC "AGENTS.md names one model entity per type, to read with awawa show before awawa new, each"
		+ "existing in the corpus"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Avant `awawa new`"
	REJECTED "A docs/_example.awawa file: the workspace walk loads it, status counts its entities"
		+ "and lint validates them"
	REJECTED "A dot-prefixed example file skipped by the walk: invisible to the tool, it would age"
		+ "without a diagnostic"
	RATIONALE "awawa new prints only the field types, not a filled example; without a model, the"
		+ "agent of PR #65 read the corpus files to find the shape"
	SOURCE "PR #68 merged, user ruling of 2026-09-13 on PR #69"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST68
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST69

DECISION ACodeCommentQuestionNamesItsCorpusEntity
	STATUS archived
	ARCHIVED_ON 2026-09-18
	SPEC "A question left as a comment in a source file is kept and names, on the next line, the"
		+ "corpus entity that carries it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.ts::// Is procedural wreck"
			+ "related to portal generator?"
	REJECTED "Deleting the comment and keeping only the corpus entity: the reader of the label"
		+ "table no longer finds the question where it applies"
	REJECTED "Keeping the comment alone, with no entity: no command reads it and status does not"
		+ "count it"
	RATIONALE "The comment is a signpost to the entity, not its home: it is useful where the table"
		+ "is read, and deleting it removes the question with it, as REFACTOR38 did; no command"
		+ "reads a comment, so the entity next to it is what reaches the next session, here the"
		+ "procedural wreck question; this is a project exception to STD-5, not a general rule,"
		+ "since the signpost is only worth an indexed entity at the other end, which only a"
		+ "project with a corpus offers"
		REF @TASK.REFACTOR38
		REF @HYPOTHESIS.ProceduralWrecksAreSpawnedByThePortalGenerator
	SOURCE "user ruling of 2026-09-14, review of PR #76"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST76

DECISION ArtifactAssetsFollowThePublishedPage
	SPEC "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/ holds the files the public feedback page for"
		+ "the awawa team links by their raw GitHub URL: the archive of the eleven reports and the"
		+ "Markdown copy of each view of the page, exported by the page or written before it"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-usage-reports.zip"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-migration-feedback.md"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-migration-2-feedback.md"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-field-report.md"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-ide-plugins-report.md"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-migration-3-feedback.md"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-feedback-overview.md"
	SPEC "The folder also holds each file the page embeds for its download button, linked by the"
		+ "same raw GitHub URL: the two versions of the specification starter"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-specification-starter.md"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/awawa-specification-starter-v2.md"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/README.md::The page embeds it for its"
			+ "download button"
	SPEC "The folder carries a README naming each file, its role and the page that links it"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/README.md"
	SPEC "No file of the folder is deleted, renamed or moved unless the page is republished without"
		+ "the matching link in the same unit of work"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/README.md::None is deleted, renamed"
	SPEC "An export the page regenerates is copied into the folder at the same republication"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-usage-reports/artifact-assets/README.md::an export the page regenerates is"
			+ "copied here"
	REJECTED "Hosting the files in a GitHub release: a release freezes one moment, whereas the"
		+ "exports follow the page at every republication"
	REJECTED "Linking the reports already under"
		+ "migration/2026_09_15-first-project-methodology-migration/: their paths were rewritten as"
		+ "relative when they were moved, whereas the archive keeps the reports as sent"
	REJECTED "A CI guard refusing a deletion in the folder: it cannot check that the page was"
		+ "adapted, only the review can"
	RATIONALE "The artifact platform does not serve an archive as a published file and blocks any"
		+ "download started by the page for a visitor outside the organization; the repository is"
		+ "the only channel for these readers, and a dead link only shows on the button, at the"
		+ "click"
	SOURCE "user ruling of 2026-09-16, session of the awawa feedback page"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST94
	SOURCE "the archive, served to the page by PR #93"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST93
	SOURCE "2026-09-18: the overview and the Migration 3 view are written as Markdown first, the"
		+ "page being built from them"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION UiSaveManagerHasNoComponentTestLayer
	REJECTED "A component test layer"
	SPEC "ui-save-manager has no component test layer: the end-to-end scenarios cover the flows and"
		+ "replace manual verification"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/playwright.config.ts::testMatch: '**/*.e2e.ts'"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	RATIONALE "A component layer would have duplicated the coverage the end-to-end scenarios"
		+ "already give on three real engines; as a consequence, a UI behaviour delivered before"
		+ "the harness existed may have stayed untested, and the harness catches it, not an"
		+ "intermediate layer"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-03, question Q6; end-to-end level opened by T23"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION UiScenariosArePlaywrightSpecsOnThreeEngines
	REJECTED "A natural-language layer above the specs"
	REJECTED "A single engine"
	REJECTED "A read double covering only the method production calls"
	SPEC "A scenario is a plain Playwright spec with no natural-language layer, so that a failing"
		+ "locator prints the accessible tree of the page"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/playwright.config.ts::testDir: './e2e'"
	SPEC "Every run covers three engines, the application handling files, blobs, object URLs and"
		+ "downloads, where engines diverge"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/playwright.config.ts::{name: 'webkit'"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/ui-tests.yml::chromium firefox webkit"
	SPEC "Scenarios and their fixtures live in the end-to-end directory of the package and carry a"
		+ "suffix the unit test runner does not collect, the fixtures being versioned next to them"
		+ "since the input directory is not"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/playwright.config.ts::testMatch: '**/*.e2e.ts'"
	SPEC "A read double covers the whole read surface of a blob, not only the method production"
		+ "calls today"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/loading-state.e2e.ts::Blob.prototype.stream"
	SPEC "The suite runs in CI only on pull requests targeting the default branch and on demand,"
		+ "and is not a required check"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/ui-tests.yml::workflow_dispatch"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST40
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT41
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	RATIONALE "Task pull requests do not trigger the suite, so making the job a required check"
		+ "would block them; local browser installation deliberately differs from CI, because"
		+ "installing with system dependencies needs privilege elevation and fails on a workstation"
		+ "without administrator rights, while the engines alone suffice; the preview command"
		+ "serves the real output of the production server, not the development server"
	SOURCE "Decided with T23, scenarios extended by T31"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST38

DECISION AControllerSpecCoversWiringNotBranches
	REJECTED "Covering business branches from controller specs"
	REJECTED "Keeping the shortest failure, which spares the parsing of the save"
	SPEC "A controller spec covers the wiring only, finer cases staying in the application,"
		+ "infrastructure and presentation specs: the three flow controller specs hold one nominal"
		+ "case and one failure case going through the error presentation, and the five section"
		+ "controller specs their single nominal case, those controllers having no failure path to"
		+ "wire"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/controllers"
	SPEC "Of two possible failures, the kept one crosses the whole wiring; a failure"
		+ "short-circuiting before the use case is not kept"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/controllers/LoadAndValidateSaveFileController.spec.ts::When"
			+ "the content is not a valid save"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST44
	RATIONALE "Replaying branches at controller level duplicates coverage already gained and makes"
		+ "every rule change cost twice; for LoadAndValidateSaveFileController the invalid"
		+ "extension is refused by the validator before the use case calls the parser and leaves"
		+ "everything after it untested, whereas the invalid content crosses validator, use case"
		+ "and error presentation, so it is the case that fails the day a link is unplugged"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-05, review of T9"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61
	SOURCE "T44, choice of the kept failure settled at implementation"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST82

DECISION ATestNeverDerivesItsInputSetFromItsSubject
	REJECTED "Iterating over the keys of the tested table and claiming exhaustiveness"
	SPEC "A test whose input set derives from the tested subject does not cover the matching"
		+ "exhaustiveness rule, and its title does not claim it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.spec.ts::worldObjectNamesByEnergyRole"
	SPEC "The partition of world object names is declared, and both directions of it are asserted"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/worldObjectNames.ts::worldObjectNamesByEnergyRole"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST43
	RATIONALE "An iteration over the keys of a table silently loses a case when an entry is"
		+ "removed, so it cannot break the rule that constrains that table; the same defect let an"
		+ "emptied constant run zero cases without a word, hence the test pinning it to its values"
	SOURCE "Decided with T25, final form settled in review"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST43

DECISION AnIllegalTestInputIsWrittenWithTsExpectError
	REJECTED "A cast to the expected type"
	SPEC "A deliberately illegal test input is written with an expected-error directive carrying a"
		+ "comment that names the invalidity, placed on the faulty field and not on the call line"
		IMPL "scripts/check-fixture-typing.ts::JUSTIFIED_TS_EXPECT_ERROR_DIRECTIVE"
		ENFORCED_BY "package.json::check:fixtures"
	SPEC "A guard walks every spec of the repository and refuses untyped fixtures"
		IMPL "scripts/check-fixture-typing.ts"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-fixture-typing.spec.ts"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST44
	RATIONALE "The directive fails the day the factory stops rejecting the data, which a cast does"
		+ "not: an illegal input test built on a cast cannot fail"
	SOURCE "Decided with T19"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST46

DECISION RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	REJECTED "Merging two guards into a single script"
	REJECTED "A configured linter instead of a dedicated script"
	REJECTED "Joining lines until parentheses balance to lift the line-by-line limit"
	SPEC "Repository guards are scripts that do not read the git history and answer in a fraction"
		+ "of a second; they are grouped behind one command and stay runnable alone"
		IMPL "package.json::check:guards"
	SPEC "What two guards share, the spec file walk, the masking of string literals and the report"
		+ "shape, is declared once in a common module, never merged into a single guard"
		IMPL "scripts/specSources.ts::maskStringLiterals"
		IMPL "scripts/specSources.ts::reportViolations"
	SPEC "The accepted limit is pinned by a test: reading is line by line, so an assertion spread"
		+ "over several lines escapes the guard"
		IMPL "scripts/check-test-assertions.spec.ts::When an assertion is spread over several lines"
	SPEC "Guards are declared as entry points of the quality audit, otherwise they are reported as"
		+ "unreachable files"
		IMPL "fallow.toml::scripts/check-test-assertions.ts"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT41
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	RATIONALE "Two merged guards would make one script with two reasons to change, one reading"
		+ "assertions and the other fixtures; the guard reads only the outermost asserted"
		+ "expression, otherwise a comparison inside a callback, a type argument or a JSX element"
		+ "passed for a fabricated boolean and broke the build on a legitimate assertion; the scope"
		+ "is the whole repository minus dependencies and build outputs, because a pattern"
		+ "restricted to packages left out the specs of the root, of the scripts and of the guard"
		+ "itself"
	SOURCE "Decided with T12; common module extracted in the review of T19"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST40
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST46

DECISION TheDoublesOfASpecShareOneFactory
	REJECTED "One double per case, each with its own recognition criterion"
	REJECTED "Leaving out of scope the sibling double of a corrected double"
	SPEC "A spec mounts its subject through a factory named with an action verb, so that each case"
		+ "states only the behaviour it changes"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.spec.ts::createUseCase"
	SPEC "The doubles of one port answer through a single indexed factory, never through as many"
		+ "inventions as there are cases"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.spec.ts::parserAnswering"
	SPEC "A double carries its weight or is removed, which is checked by a mutation forcing it to"
		+ "accept everything and counting the tests that fail"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.spec.ts"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST44
	RATIONALE "Five doubles of the same spec each invented their own way to recognise a save and"
		+ "did not even agree on what identifies it; leaving the sibling double out of scope is"
		+ "what made the remaining one look arbitrary"
	SOURCE "Third review pass of T28"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST59

DECISION EveryPublishedCommandHasARealProcessTest
	REJECTED "A dedicated CI job instead of a test"
	REJECTED "Observing only the exit code"
	SPEC "Every command the repository publishes has a test that launches it as a real process from"
		+ "the test runner, never a dedicated CI job"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.node.spec.js::spawn("
		IMPL "packages/cli-validate/cli/validate-cli.node.spec.js::spawn("
	SPEC "The merge cases assert the produced content, not only the exit code"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.node.spec.js::should carry the contribution of both"
			+ "saves into the merged file"
	SPEC "Each input save unlocks a group no other save unlocks, so the produced file names the"
		+ "saves that actually reached the merge engine"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.node.spec.js::GROUP_UNLOCKED_BY_SAVE_B_ONLY"
	RATIONALE "An in-memory spec proves that a use case behaves as intended, never that a binary"
		+ "starts: three defects went through that gap, one of them a command broken for three days"
		+ "and seven pull requests; the loss of a whole section on a save prefixed with a byte"
		+ "order mark exited with code zero announcing a success; a guard placed in the test runner"
		+ "covers the workstation and CI at once"
	SOURCE "Decided with T22"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST45

DECISION MockIsolationIsAGlobalPreload
	REJECTED "A cleanup block per spec file"
	SPEC "Isolation of doubles is global: a test runner preload restores and clears the doubles"
		+ "after every test, never a cleanup block per spec"
		IMPL "testing/testIsolation.ts::enforceTestIsolation"
		ENFORCED_BY "testIsolation.spec.ts"
	SPEC "The preload is declared at the root and in every package, all calling the same isolation"
		+ "function"
		IMPL "bunfig.toml::preload"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/bunfig.toml::preload"
		IMPL "testSetup.ts::enforceTestIsolation()"
	RATIONALE "The test runner configuration file is resolved from the current directory only,"
		+ "without walking up, so a single declaration at the root leaves any run started from a"
		+ "package without isolation; the reset primitive announced by the types does not exist at"
		+ "run time in the version in use"
	SOURCE "Decision of 2026-09-05, review of T9"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

DECISION NoSaveIsCommittedToThePublicRepository
	REJECTED "Committing a reference save to the public repository"
	REJECTED "A registry of temporary directories shared between the tests of a file"
	SPEC "No save is committed to the public repository: specs that need one generate their"
		+ "fixtures at run time, write them to a temporary directory and remove it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.fs.adapters.spec.js::fs.mkdtemp"
	SPEC "Each test creates its own temporary directory before and removes it after, never a shared"
		+ "registry that is emptied"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.fs.adapters.spec.js::await fs.rm(directory"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT41
	RATIONALE "A shared registry leaves a spy on the global object for the rest of the test process"
		+ "when nobody restores it, which happened"
	SOURCE "Decided with T22; temporary directory form settled in the review of T36"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST45

DECISION TheAdapterContractIsTestedOnceAgainstEachAdapter
	REJECTED "Two independent specs, one per adapter"
	REJECTED "Asserting an adapter against its own sibling function"
	SPEC "The cases of the file access contract are listed once and run against each adapter,"
		+ "asserting against the file system and never against the sibling function of the same"
		+ "adapter"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.fs.adapters.spec.js::describe.each(FILE_ACCESS_ADAPTERS)"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.fs.adapters.spec.js::expect(await"
			+ "fs.readFile(filePath"
	SPEC "Behaviours whose semantics diverge by design stay in the per-adapter specs"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.node.spec.js"
		IMPL "packages/shared-platforms/platform.bun.spec.js"
	RATIONALE "Two independent specs per adapter are exactly what let a read divergence between the"
		+ "two adapters through"
	SOURCE "Review of T18"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST33

DECISION AScenarioReadsTheDownloadThroughTheNodeFileApi
	REJECTED "Settling for the presence of the link and the file name it offers"
	REJECTED "Declaring the Node types in the type-check project of the sources directory"
	REJECTED "Asserting the whole downloaded file: the output of a merge cannot be written as a"
		+ "literal and comparing it would replay the core-mapping rules"
	REJECTED "A single function returning the downloaded content: the file name scenario asserts on"
		+ "the download itself and not on its content, so the two gestures stay two functions"
	SPEC "The merge scenario reads the downloaded file from disk through the Node file API, the"
		+ "download being an artifact of the runner and not of the page, and asserts it on a"
		+ "discriminating field, not on the whole file"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/merge.e2e.ts::import {readFile} from 'node:fs/promises';"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/merge.e2e.ts::mergedSaveDisplayName"
	SPEC "The type-check project of the end-to-end directory declares the Node types next to those"
		+ "of the runner, while the project of the sources directory still declares only browser"
		+ "libraries"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/tsconfig.json::@playwright/test"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/tsconfig.json::vite/client"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST40
	RATIONALE "A scenario file runs in the runner and not in the browser: denying it the Node API"
		+ "would have left the content check to the name of the link, which the task card"
		+ "explicitly forbids; this is not a widened quality gate but the declaration of the real"
		+ "runtime of a scope, the repository rule being that a type-check project declares only"
		+ "what its scope is entitled to; the content is asserted on the display name the merge"
		+ "writes into the produced save, which neither source carries, the discriminating field"
		+ "that tells the merged file from its inputs without replaying a merge rule"
	SOURCE "T24, 2026-09-14"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST75

DECISION AScenarioFixtureIsNamedByContentAndVerdict
	REJECTED "role_context_expected in three segments: the role varies per scenario, and with two"
		+ "fixtures the context segment would be empty or false"
	REJECTED "Keeping valid-save.json and companion-save.json: the first does not say what the save"
		+ "carries, the second names a role"
	SPEC "A scenario fixture is named content_verdict.json: what the save carries that no other"
		+ "carries, an underscore, then the validator verdict, valid or invalid, words within a"
		+ "segment being separated by a hyphen, and the convention is written next to the fixtures"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/README.md::## Naming"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/other-player_valid.json"
	SPEC "The role of a fixture in a scenario is not in its name: it lives in the variable that"
		+ "binds it and in the README of the fixtures directory"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/README.md::## `baseline_valid.json`"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST40
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT41
	RATIONALE "A role segment does not hold, since baseline_valid.json is both the displayed save"
		+ "of the display scenarios and save A of the merge scenario, so a role segment would lie"
		+ "or force a duplicate; content and verdict are the two stable properties of a fixture,"
		+ "and the ones that multiply as scenarios multiply; the merged file name derives from both"
		+ "input names, so the renaming lengthens the expected constant of the merge scenario,"
		+ "which thereby names its two sources"
	SOURCE "Review, user ruling of 2026-09-14, T24"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST75

DECISION AUiScenarioAssertsWhatTheScreenShows
	REJECTED "Asserting the complete message the rule produces"
	REJECTED "An invalid fixture accumulating several violations: the expectation stops being a"
		+ "location and becomes the list of violated rules again"
	SPEC "A UI scenario asserts what the screen shows of a validation message, its presence, its"
		+ "location and the fact that it is a sentence, never the text the rule produced"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/validation-errors.e2e.ts::toContainText(errorLocationInTheSave)"
	SPEC "A warning is asserted on a discriminating fragment of its sentence and on the absence of"
		+ "the code it carries inside the application"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/warnings.e2e.ts::not.toContainText(legacyFormatWarningCode)"
	SPEC "An invalid fixture carries a single violation, located on one record, so the expectation"
		+ "of the scenario is the location alone"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/negative-gauge_invalid.json"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST40
	RATIONALE "An invalid fixture shows a message without reasserting the rule that produces it,"
		+ "otherwise the scenario duplicates on three engines a coverage core-mapping already"
		+ "holds; the location and the choice of a sentence over a code are presentation decisions,"
		+ "so asserting them on screen covers what only end-to-end covers and nothing the rule"
		+ "decides"
	SOURCE "T40, 2026-09-14"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST78

DECISION ALoadingStateIsObservedByHoldingTheFileRead
	REJECTED "Asserting the indicator without holding the read: the assertion becomes intermittent"
	REJECTED "Slowing production down or adding a test hook to it to make the state observable"
	REJECTED "A hold placed on the only read method production calls"
		REF @DECISION.UiScenariosArePlaywrightSpecsOnThreeEngines
	SPEC "A loading state scenario holds the read of the chosen file from the test on the whole"
		+ "read surface of a blob, then releases it explicitly, so the busy state is observed"
		+ "instead of raced"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/loading-state.e2e.ts::Blob.prototype.arrayBuffer"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/loading-state.e2e.ts::releaseTheHeldFileReads"
	SPEC "The hold is installed by a page initialisation script and released by a call exposed on"
		+ "the window, production being untouched"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/loading-state.e2e.ts::page.addInitScript"
	SPEC "The end of the loading state of the display flow is asserted by the rendered button and"
		+ "the data on screen, not by the absence of an indicator, each visualisation section"
		+ "carrying its own"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/loading-state.e2e.ts::should end the busy state and hand"
			+ "the button back"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST40
	RATIONALE "A fixture of a few kilobytes is read faster than the first poll of the runner:"
		+ "without a hold the scenario passes when it catches the indicator and breaks when it"
		+ "misses it, an intermittent test rather than coverage; the hold was checked by"
		+ "neutralising the release, which makes both end-of-state scenarios fail and proves they"
		+ "do not assert on a screen already reached"
	SOURCE "T40, 2026-09-14"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST78

DECISION TheFirstDescribeNamesTheRuleTheSpecCovers
	REJECTED "Keeping the function name prefixed with a hash"
	REJECTED "Removing only the technical prefix, which gave two files the same first describe"
	SPEC "The first describe of a spec names, in business language, the rule the file covers, even"
		+ "when the spec exercises it through the caller of that rule"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/determineSaveOrder.spec.ts::describe('Determine"
			+ "save order'"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST43
	RATIONALE "determineSaveOrder.spec.ts announced itself by its function name prefixed with a"
		+ "hash; removing only the technical prefix left a title already carried by"
		+ "mergeSaveSections.spec.ts, and two files under one name"
	SOURCE "T43, re-audit of the 2026-09-07 survey"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST79

DECISION ScenarioSuiteArtifactsAreAlreadyIgnored
	REJECTED "Pointing the runner output to an already ignored directory: all three already are,"
		+ "and moving the output would change a working configuration for a defect that does not"
		+ "exist"
	REJECTED "Adding two ignore rules: they are already written in .gitignore"
	SPEC "playwright-report/, test-results/ and blob-report/ are ignored without anchor, hence at"
		+ "any depth of the repository, so the scenario suite needs no rule added and no output"
		+ "moved"
		IMPL ".gitignore::playwright-report/"
		IMPL ".gitignore::test-results/"
		IMPL ".gitignore::blob-report/"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	RATIONALE "Measured on 2026-09-15: with the three directories created and populated under"
		+ "packages/ui-save-manager, the porcelain status with all untracked files returns nothing,"
		+ "and check-ignore names the .gitignore rules; blob-report/ is the output a sharded run"
		+ "merges, and would be the next omission of a survey counting only two directories"
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-15, wave 4 launch commit"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST80

DECISION ScenarioFixturesAreGeneratedAndReplayedByAGuard
	REJECTED "Keeping the recipes in the README and having the guard run its code blocks: the"
		+ "documentation format would become a program contract"
	REJECTED "Versioning a fingerprint per fixture instead of replaying the generator"
	REJECTED "Duplicating the file walk in the guard rather than parameterising the one of the"
		+ "common module"
	REJECTED "Merging this guard with check:fixtures, which reads the typing of spec fixtures: two"
		+ "reasons to change for one script"
	SPEC "A script declares every scenario fixture and is the only place that says how each is"
		+ "built; bun run generate:scenario-fixtures writes them"
		IMPL "scripts/generate-scenario-fixtures.ts::SCENARIO_FIXTURES"
		IMPL "package.json::generate:scenario-fixtures"
	SPEC "The guard replays the generator in memory and compares byte for byte with the versioned"
		+ "file, storing no fingerprint and reading no git history; it fails on any byte difference"
		+ "and on a declared fixture the repository does not carry"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-fixtures.ts"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-scenario-fixtures.spec.ts"
	SPEC "The same guard refuses a scenario file that names the input directory in a path, which"
		+ "makes the independence from that directory executable"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-fixtures.ts::INPUT_DIRECTORY_PATH"
	SPEC "The segment boundary before input/ excludes word characters, the dot and the hyphen,"
		+ "never the slash, since a slash opens a segment and must let the match through"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-fixtures.spec.ts::a separator opening a fresh path segment"
	SPEC "The README of the fixtures directory keeps the naming convention and the role of each"
		+ "fixture, and carries no executable recipe"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/README.md::## Naming"
	SPEC "The shared walk takes the pattern as a parameter, so a scenario guard does not write a"
		+ "second one"
		IMPL "scripts/specSources.ts::readOwnSourceFiles"
	SPEC "The guard is grouped behind check:guards and declared as an entry point of the audit"
		IMPL "package.json::check:scenario-fixtures"
		IMPL "fallow.toml::scripts/check-scenario-fixtures.ts"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT41
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	RATIONALE "The generator extracted from the README recipes reproduces the four versioned"
		+ "fixtures byte for byte, and the scenarios pass on the three engines with the input/ link"
		+ "removed; replaying the generator rather than comparing a fingerprint makes the guard"
		+ "fail where the defect is, the generator having changed and the fixture not, instead of"
		+ "only saying that two numbers differ; the slash was first in the class of the lookbehind,"
		+ "so paths starting with ${process.cwd()}/input/ or /home/.../input/ passed the guard"
		+ "although their input/ segment is written out in the line, and the hyphen alone suffices"
		+ "to rule out user-input/; the accepted limit is that scenarios are still read line by"
		+ "line, so a path assembled at run time escapes the input directory check; the walk of"
		+ "specSources takes the pattern as a parameter so that readOwnSpecFiles delegates to it,"
		+ "following the shape of the repository guards"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	SOURCE "T41 and its review"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST81

DECISION TheSharedWalkFilterIsNamedAfterWhatItFilters
	REJECTED "Keeping isOwnSpecFile and renaming after the wave is merged: the cost avoided is a"
		+ "trivial conflict, paid for by a false name in the base and by a deferred task nobody"
		+ "claims"
	REJECTED "Also renaming readOwnSpecFiles and its pattern: their scope is indeed the specs,"
		+ "their name is accurate"
	SPEC "The filter of the shared walk is named isOwnSourceFile, since it discards generated"
		+ "directories from every walked file, spec or scenario, and its spec names it the same way"
		IMPL "scripts/specSources.ts::isOwnSourceFile"
		IMPL "scripts/specSources.spec.ts::describe('isOwnSourceFile'"
	SPEC "readOwnSpecFiles and SPEC_FILES_PATTERN keep the word spec, as they alone serve specs"
		+ "only"
		IMPL "scripts/specSources.ts::readOwnSpecFiles"
		IMPL "scripts/specSources.ts::SPEC_FILES_PATTERN"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT41
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	RATIONALE "The renaming is done in the pull request that created the mismatch, not in a commit"
		+ "deferred after the wave is merged: deferring left a false name in the base for the whole"
		+ "wave, against a one-line rebase conflict on a stacked branch that is rebased anyway"
	SOURCE "Review of T41"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST81

DECISION AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
	REJECTED "Writing a second walk in the guard, its first state: the common walk was already"
		+ "parameterised, and two walks would have given the duplication the guard family rules out"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	REJECTED "Widening the fixed pattern of the common walk to scenario files rather than passing"
		+ "the pattern as a parameter: the two guards reading specs would have started reading"
		+ "scenarios and applying rules written for unit specs, the shape of assertions and the"
		+ "typing of fixtures"
	REJECTED "Deriving the ambiguous label from the message modules by keeping any value exported"
		+ "by more than one module: the guard would take a second reason to change, which the guard"
		+ "family rules out, for a single label shared today"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	REJECTED "Recognising a CSS selector by the shape of its literal, a leading dot, hash or"
		+ "bracket: a legitimate expectation such as getByRole('button', {name: '#3'}) would be"
		+ "refused"
	REJECTED "Refusing every Playwright shortcut taking a selector regardless of its receiver:"
		+ "setInputFiles, click and press are the very gestures of the delivered scenarios when a"
		+ "locator receives them"
	SPEC "check:locators refuses in scenario files a test id, a CSS selector, a reference"
		+ "screenshot and the label the busy indicator shares with the hydration fallback, and its"
		+ "line-by-line limit is pinned by a test that names it"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.ts"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts::the accepted limit of a line reading being"
			+ "that it never joins two lines"
	SPEC "The guard writes no walk: it passes its pattern to the shared walk of specSources and"
		+ "takes the literal masking and the report shape from it"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.ts::import {maskStringLiterals, readOwnSourceFiles,"
			+ "reportViolations} from './specSources.ts';"
	SPEC "Two patterns are read on the masked line, the refused call being code, and two on the raw"
		+ "line, since masking erases the very literal they look for"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.ts::maskStringLiterals"
	SPEC "A Playwright shortcut taking a selector is refused only when page is its immediate"
		+ "receiver"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.ts::SELECTOR_TAKING_PAGE_ACTION"
	SPEC "The guard runs alone and grouped behind the guards command"
		IMPL "package.json::check:locators"
	SPEC "The guard and its spec are declared as entry points of the quality audit"
		IMPL "fallow.toml::scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	RATIONALE "Before the guard, none of the five existing guards read what a scenario asserts: the"
		+ "two reading test content walked a pattern fixed on spec files that never meets a .e2e.ts"
		+ "file, and the two walking packages read only import specifiers; replayed on the five"
		+ "delivered scenarios the guard reports nothing, since they already designate by role,"
		+ "label or displayed sentence, and four patterns deliberately introduced in merge.e2e.ts"
		+ "make it fail line by line; the fourth pattern is the one the loading scenario ruling"
		+ "calls for, naming this guard as the place where a label shared between two states is"
		+ "called ambiguous; the guard follows the shape of the existing guards, with no git"
		+ "history read, an answer in a fraction of a second, a standalone and grouped run and a"
		+ "line-by-line limit pinned by a test"
		REF @DECISION.ScenarioFixturesAreGeneratedAndReplayedByAGuard
		REF @DECISION.AUiScenarioAssertsWhatTheScreenShows
		REF @DECISION.LoadingScenariosLocateTheSpinnerByRoleNeverByLabel
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	SOURCE "T42, 2026-09-15"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST83

DECISION TheAmbiguousLabelIsPinnedInTheGuardSpec
	REJECTED "Deriving the label from the message modules inside the guard itself: ruled out for"
		+ "the guard, and the pinning does not need it to stay faithful over time"
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
	REJECTED "Leaving the constant alone: nothing would signal the drift"
	REJECTED "Asserting both modules against the literal 'Loading...' in the spec instead of the"
		+ "exported constant: rewriting a module would be seen, but the link with what the guard"
		+ "looks for would stay unstated, and the constant could drift alone"
	SPEC "The ambiguous label constant is exported by the locator guard and pinned in its spec"
		+ "against the imported displayRouteLoadingLabel and spinnerLoadingLabel, so rewriting"
		+ "either fails bun test instead of silently disarming the fourth pattern"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.ts::AMBIGUOUS_BUSY_LABEL"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts::expect(AMBIGUOUS_BUSY_LABEL).toBe(displayRouteLoadingLabel);"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts::expect(AMBIGUOUS_BUSY_LABEL).toBe(spinnerLoadingLabel);"
	SPEC "The guard itself still reads only scenarios; its spec is what imports the two message"
		+ "modules"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts::import {spinnerLoadingLabel} from"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	RATIONALE "The constant was a third copy of the label that nothing tied to the two modules; the"
		+ "rejected clause of the guard ruling covers deriving the label in the guard, which would"
		+ "give it a second reason to change, whereas the spec already changes with the guard, so"
		+ "the count of reasons to change does not move; a scripts file importing a package module"
		+ "is already the repository shape, generate-scenario-fixtures.ts importing"
		+ "createSaveRecords from shared-save-processing, and check:dependencies walks only"
		+ "packages/* while the import is relative, so it is doubly out of its scope"
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
	SOURCE "Review of T42"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST83

DECISION RefusedShortcutsAreReadFromThePlaywrightApi
	REJECTED "Adding frameLocator to the list of page shortcuts: it would then be refused only on"
		+ "page, whereas a locator receiving it takes the same raw selector"
	REJECTED "Refusing page.frame because it takes a string: its argument is a frame name or URL,"
		+ "and the guard would become wrong"
	REJECTED "Rewriting the list by hand at every version upgrade: it is read off the installed"
		+ "types, a Page method whose first argument is a selector being the only criterion"
	SPEC "The list of shortcuts the locator guard refuses is read off the installed playwright-core"
		+ "types, never written from memory: every Page method whose first argument is a selector"
		+ "is in it, and it is refused when page is its immediate receiver"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.ts::SELECTOR_TAKING_PAGE_ACTION"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts::await page.dragAndDrop('.merge-result',"
			+ "'.trash');"
	SPEC "frameLocator belongs to the receiver-less pattern next to .locator(, its argument being a"
		+ "raw selector whatever the receiver, Page, Locator or FrameLocator"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.ts::SELECTOR_QUERY"
		IMPL "scripts/check-scenario-locators.spec.ts::frameLocator('iframe.preview')"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT42
	RATIONALE "dragAndDrop, setChecked, inputValue and frameLocator were missing from the delivered"
		+ "guard; read on playwright-core 1.63.0, Page has thirty methods whose first argument is a"
		+ "selector, and those four were the only absent ones; frameLocator also escaped the"
		+ "receiver-less pattern, since .locator( requires a dot and a lower-case l; page.frame"
		+ "stays out of the guard, its argument naming a frame by name or URL, not an element of"
		+ "the page, and the limit is kept, not widened: Frame carries the same API as Page, so"
		+ "page.frame('name').click('.x') escapes the guard under the immediate receiver rule"
		+ "already decided, and lifting it would refuse the very gestures of the delivered"
		+ "scenarios"
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
	SOURCE "Review of T42"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST83

DECISION TheSchemaGovernsEveryAreaFromTheDocsRoot
	SPEC "Every SCHEMA, FIELDSET and SHAPE declaration of the workspace lives in docs/_schema.awawa"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::SCHEMA *"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::La spécification du projet est le corpus awawa"
	SPEC "An area directory under docs holds entity files only, one per type, lower-case plural"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/sections.awawa"
	REJECTED "A _schema.awawa per area: the second one would either duplicate SCHEMA * or declare a"
		+ "second, which one workspace does not admit"
	REJECTED "Keeping the schema inside the methodology area: it governs both areas, so it would"
		+ "sit under the one it is not about"
	RATIONALE "The tool reads no file name, so the layout costs nothing to the commands and is"
		+ "chosen for the reader; a declaration that governs two areas is placed above both. The"
		+ "move was priced before it was made: one IMPL anchor and three path mentions in"
		+ "AGENTS.md, references being by identity"
	SOURCE "2026-09-17"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION TheSpecificationAreaPivotsOnTheRule
	SPEC "A question about the product starts from a RULE: the pivot of the specification area is"
		+ "RULE, as the pivot of the methodology area is TASK"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Chaque aire a son pivot"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::SCHEMA RULE"
	SPEC "No specification type carries a delivery state: what is not built yet is a TASK, never a"
		+ "RULE, a SECTION, a COMMAND, a HYPOTHESIS or a DATATABLE"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::FIELD STATUS active|archived"
	REJECTED "SECTION as the pivot: it declares no reference field, so its context package is the"
		+ "entity alone — 1 entity and 6 lines, against 4 entities and 26 lines for a rule,"
		+ "measured on the probe area; the two reading questions that start from a section are"
		+ "served by the CONSTRAINED_BY footer context already prints"
	REJECTED "A STATUS ladder with an implemented rung on the pivot: a rule is true or false, not"
		+ "delivered, and COMMAND.IMPL and RULE.SPEC.ATTESTED_BY are REQUIRED anchors that nothing"
		+ "unbuilt resolves"
	REJECTED "One pivot for the whole workspace: the two areas answer two questions, and hanging a"
		+ "specification entity on a TASK is the edge already refused"
	RATIONALE "The pivot is a convention for readers: the tool knows no pivot, so the choice is"
		+ "priced on what context returns from each candidate. RULE is where the outgoing edges"
		+ "leave — APPLIES_TO_SECTION, VALUES_FROM, ASSUMES — and the only incoming one, APPLIED_BY"
		+ "from COMMAND, is printed in the footer of that same package. COMMAND returns a larger"
		+ "package, 5 entities and 31 lines, but only reaches what a command applies, and most"
		+ "questions are not about a command"
		REF @DECISION.TheSchemaGovernsEveryAreaFromTheDocsRoot
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION TheEraIsNotTheArchive
	SPEC "A SECTION the game stopped writing stays active and carries HOLDS_FOR legacy; STATUS"
		+ "archived is written only when the project stops supporting what the entity describes"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::FIELDSET Era"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::L'ère n'est pas l'archive"
	SPEC "An entity lints clean before it is archived, and nothing active still points at it"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::WHEN STATUS archived"
	SPEC "PURGE keeps its default on a specification entity: the cleanup pass deletes an archived"
		+ "entity once the delay has run and the incoming count status TYPE prints is zero"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::FIELD PURGE true|false"
	REJECTED "Archiving a section the game removed: its rules still bind the saves written before"
		+ "the removal, and archiving would remove its body from every context package that cites"
		+ "it"
	REJECTED "PURGE false by default on the five specification types: it turns the archive into the"
		+ "history the corpus refuses to hold"
	RATIONALE "GATE suppressed prices the archive dearly, measured on the probe area: an archived"
		+ "SECTION declaring HOLDS_FOR current without INDEX lints clean, an archived RULE with"
		+ "DOMAIN merge and none of the three fields that case requires lints clean, and an"
		+ "archived entity's dangling reference and unresolvable anchor raise neither L004 nor L016"
		+ "— only the fields of the WHEN STATUS archived block itself, ARCHIVED_ON and PURGE, are"
		+ "still checked. Archiving is therefore an act on an entity already clean, never a way to"
		+ "quiet one. It also costs the readers: context on an active entity prints // suppressed"
		+ "in place of the archived entity it points at, so archiving a still-cited entity silently"
		+ "shrinks every package that cites it"
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION AnAnchorNamesAFileTrackedByGit
	SPEC "Every anchor of the corpus names a file git tracks; a path under input, output or"
		+ ".do-not-commit is never anchored"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Une ancre nomme un fichier suivi par git"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::the committed fixture, JSON Schema, test or document that proves"
			+ "the index"
	SPEC "A statement about the save is attested by a committed witness: a fixture of"
		+ "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures, a JSON Schema of"
		+ "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas, a test, or a document of docs"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/fixtures/legacy-format_valid.json"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/save-file.schema.json"
	REJECTED "Anchoring an attestation on a reference save: the saves are not committed, carry the"
		+ "real names of the players and weigh eight megabytes, so the anchor resolves for its"
		+ "author alone"
	REJECTED "Leaving the rule unwritten and letting the continuous integration find it: the"
		+ "finding then names a clone, not the line that was written"
	RATIONALE "L016 resolves an anchor against the workspace root and tests existence on disk"
		+ "alone, git being never consulted: measured on a probe workspace that is not a git"
		+ "repository at all and resolves its anchors normally. The corpus carries 487 anchors and"
		+ "none of them points at an ignored directory today; what creates the risk is"
		+ "SECTION.ATTESTED_BY, REQUIRED on the twelve sections still to be written, whose natural"
		+ "witness is one of the eight save files that are not committed"
		REF @DECISION.NoSaveIsCommittedToThePublicRepository
		REF @DECISION.ThePrivateContextHoldsOnlySavesAndPlans
	SOURCE "Review of the target schema, 2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION AGameReleaseIsCitedAsASource
	SPEC "What was observed in the game is sourced by a GAME_RELEASE entity named by the version"
		+ "the game prints, 2.102 today"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::SCHEMA GAME_RELEASE"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Une observation dans le jeu cite sa version"
	SPEC "No type of the specification area carries the game version as a field of its own"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::SCHEMA RULE"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::SCHEMA HYPOTHESIS"
	REJECTED "A GAME_VERSION field on RULE: the version qualifies the observation, not the"
		+ "obligation, so it would be written on every rule and mean the version of the last"
		+ "reading, which is what a SOURCE already says"
	REJECTED "The version in the SOURCE prose alone: SOURCE.REF is REQUIRED, and an observation"
		+ "made in the game has no entity to point at, so the line would have to cite the private"
		+ "context or a wiki page that did not carry it"
	REJECTED "A PascalCase name such as V2102: the dot is the name segment separator, so NAME"
		+ "version_segment on the type admits 2.102 as it is written and refuses 2.102b, measured"
	RATIONALE "S1 lists the game itself among the places the specification is read from, and it is"
		+ "the one place with no citable entity. The version is the falsifiable part: the 639 keys"
		+ "of the community label file target 2.102, and the wiki cross-check of 2026-09-09 was"
		+ "made against that build. The type carries no field: its identity is the version, and"
		+ "NAME version_segment checks it"
		REF @DECISION.AnExternalPageIsCitedAtTheAddressRead
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION AnExternalPageIsCitedAtTheAddressRead
	SPEC "A page read outside the repository is cited by a URL entity whose LOCATION is the address"
		+ "read, pinned on a commit where the host offers one"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::SCHEMA URL"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::une page lue dehors cite son adresse"
	SPEC "The day a page was read is written in the prose of the SOURCE that cites it, never on the"
		+ "URL entity"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::FIELD SOURCE string"
	SPEC "The provenance of one row of a DATATABLE is a column of the table, never an entity"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::SCHEMA DATATABLE"
	REJECTED "A PROJECT entity for the mod repository akarnokd/ThePlanetCrafterMods: PROJECT"
		+ "records a repository and no commit, the corpus cites no pull request of that repository,"
		+ "and the 639 keys must be pinned at the commit they were read from"
	REJECTED "A READ_ON date on URL: the wiki pages of the energy values were read on several days,"
		+ "so the date belongs to the citation and not to the page"
	REJECTED "One URL entity for the wiki as a whole, the page named in prose: the address is what"
		+ "the type exists to carry"
	RATIONALE "Two of the places S1 inventories are external pages: the community wiki, some thirty"
		+ "pages of it, and the English label file of the (UI) English Plus Translation mod, whose"
		+ "permalink pins the commit read. Neither needs a type of its own: SHAPE url already"
		+ "validates LOCATION, and a per-row wiki page stays a column of the JSON table, which is"
		+ "what keeps the 105 energy rows out of the corpus"
		REF @DECISION.AGameReleaseIsCitedAsASource
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION AFieldLegalInOneStateIsDeclaredInThatStateAlone
	SPEC "A field whose legality depends on the value of another field is declared inside the WHEN"
		+ "block of that value and nowhere else"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::WHEN DOMAIN merge"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Un champ légal dans un seul état n'est déclaré que là"
	SPEC "A field legal in several states is repeated in the block of each of them"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::WHEN HOLDS_FOR both"
	REJECTED "Declaring the field at type level and adding REQUIRED in the WHEN block: the field"
		+ "then stays legal in every state, WHEN being monotonic, and a legacy section carrying a"
		+ "current INDEX lints clean"
	RATIONALE "Measured on the probe workspace: with INDEX and LEGACY_INDEX declared only in the"
		+ "era blocks, a HOLDS_FOR legacy section carrying INDEX 9 raises L003 field INDEX is not"
		+ "declared on SECTION, and a DOMAIN format rule carrying CONFLICT and RESOLUTION raises"
		+ "two more; the same workspace with the S4 declarations lints clean on both. Repeating"
		+ "INDEX in WHEN HOLDS_FOR current and WHEN HOLDS_FOR both raises no L013. It is the shape"
		+ "SCHEMA * already gives ARCHIVED_ON and PURGE, legal only under WHEN STATUS archived"
		REF @DECISION.TheEraIsNotTheArchive
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION ASectionIsWrittenWithTheRuleThatCitesIt
	SPEC "a SECTION whose era is current or both is added in the same pull request as at least one"
		+ "RULE naming it under APPLIES_TO_SECTION"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::INCOMING CONSTRAINED_BY"
		ENFORCED_BY "docs/_schema.awawa::INCOMING CONSTRAINED_BY"
	SPEC "the twelve sections of the save were written paired with their rule, in save index order,"
		+ "the legacy section last"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/sections.awawa"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/rules.awawa"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.ASaveHasElevenSectionsTheLastReservedAndEmpty
	REJECTED "writing the twelve sections first and their rules afterwards: L026 fires on every"
		+ "uncited section, so the corpus would not lint between the two writes and no intermediate"
		+ "commit would be possible"
	REJECTED "dropping INCOMING CONSTRAINED_BY to make a lone section legal: a section the game"
		+ "writes today that no rule constrains is a hole in the specification that nothing else"
		+ "reports"
	RATIONALE "The obligation is not a style preference: it is what makes the specification"
		+ "complete by construction, since a section with no rule is the shape a forgotten"
		+ "obligation takes"
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION AValueTableIsRecordedOnceItsFileExists
	SPEC "a DATATABLE is written only when the JSON file and the JSON Schema its TABLE and"
		+ "JSON_SCHEMA name are tracked by git"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::FIELD JSON_SCHEMA anchor"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/tasks.awawa::the product value tables become JSON"
			+ "files with a JSON Schema each"
	REJECTED "creating the JSON files in the step that writes the first entities, the TypeScript"
		+ "modules keeping their rows: every value would have two homes until the rewiring landed,"
		+ "which is the duplication the tables are being moved to end"
	REJECTED "writing the five DATATABLE against the TypeScript modules: TABLE names the file"
		+ "holding the rows, and a module that restates them is not that file"
	UNTIL @TASK.CHORE52
	RATIONALE "The rule generalises beyond the tables: an anchor field that is REQUIRED makes the"
		+ "entity wait for the artefact, and the wait is carried by a task rather than by a"
		+ "placeholder anchor"
		REF @DECISION.AnAnchorNamesAFileTrackedByGit
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION ADocumentIsDeletedOnlyWhenEveryCitationIsRepointed
	SPEC "A document of docs/ is deleted only once every statement it carried has another home and"
		+ "every citation of it, inside the corpus and outside, has been repointed"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Un document de `docs/` n'est supprimé qu'une fois toutes ses citations"
			+ "repointées"
	SPEC "The citations outside the corpus are counted before the deletion, the lint resolving the"
		+ "corpus anchors and nothing else"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::grep -rn '<nom du document>' ."
	SPEC "A code comment cites the corpus entity, never the document"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Un commentaire de code cite alors l'entité, jamais"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/determineSaveOrder.ts"
	REJECTED "Relying on L016 alone: it resolves the anchors the corpus carries and reads no code"
		+ "comment, no README link and no other document"
	REJECTED "Deleting the document first and finding its citations afterwards: a comment naming a"
		+ "file that no longer exists is read as a place to go, and nothing reports it"
	REJECTED "Keeping the document as a redirection page: it is a second home again, and the walk"
		+ "deleted the first one to end exactly that"
	RATIONALE "Measured on 2026-09-18 at the deletion of docs/game-rules.md, 219 lines whose thirty"
		+ "GR-* rules had all become a SPEC of one of the fourteen RULE DOMAIN merge: the gate"
		+ "raised six L016, five IMPL and one SEEN_IN, and said nothing of the twenty-four code"
		+ "comments in twenty-one files, the thirteen README lines and the two links from"
		+ "docs/save-format.md and docs/energy-levels.md — forty-five citation sites of which the"
		+ "tool saw six"
	SOURCE "2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION TheMergedSaveDisplayNameComesFromTheCaller
	REJECTED "Keeping it as a SPEC of @RULE.SaveConfigurationComesFromSaveA, where it was first"
		+ "written: neither save's saveDisplayName is read, so the obligation settles no"
		+ "disagreement between the two saves and no save can contradict it"
		REF @RULE.SaveConfigurationComesFromSaveA
	REJECTED "Carrying save A's saveDisplayName into the merged save: the name would designate a"
		+ "folder the merge did not produce"
	SPEC "saveDisplayName is overridden with the value the caller passes to the merge, taken from"
		+ "the input folder name in the command"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeSaveConfigurations.ts::{...saveConfiguration,"
			+ "saveDisplayName}"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeSaveConfigurations.spec.ts::should"
			+ "use the saveDisplayName parameter and take save configuration from save A"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RATIONALE "The two inputs are not consulted at all: the display name is an argument of the"
		+ "merge, so the obligation belongs to what the caller owes the merge and not to how two"
		+ "saves are reconciled. Sanitizing it is still owed, and stays where it was recorded"
	SOURCE "Reclassified from GR-CFG-2 of docs/game-rules.md on 2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION MissingPlayerFieldsAreWrittenAsZero
	REJECTED "Keeping it as a SPEC of @RULE.PlayersAreDeduplicatedByName, where it was first"
		+ "written: the defaulting applies to one entry whatever the other save holds, so it"
		+ "settles no disagreement between the two saves"
		REF @RULE.PlayersAreDeduplicatedByName
	REJECTED "Writing the merged entry without the fields the source entry omits, as the game does:"
		+ "the merged save would then be written in a shape older than the one the game writes"
	SPEC "cameraView, totalCraftedObjects and totalTerraTokenEarned are written as 0 when the"
		+ "source entry omits them"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergePlayers.ts::cameraView: 0"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergePlayers.spec.ts::should"
			+ "default the missing fields to 0"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RESTS_ON @RULE.APlayerEntryMayOmitTheFieldsAddedByALaterUpdate
	RATIONALE "The save may omit the three fields and the merge must still write one shape; zero is"
		+ "the value the game itself starts them at, so the merged entry reads as an entry of a"
		+ "save that never earned any"
	SOURCE "Reclassified from GR-PLAYER-4 of docs/game-rules.md on 2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION TheDomainOfARuleIsDecidedByWhetherThePlayWouldChange
	REJECTED "Reading DOMAIN game as any statement about the simulated world, whatever the save"
		+ "does with it: the encoding of a game state would then be a game rule, and"
		+ "@RULE.APlanetNumericIdIsStableAcrossSaves and"
		+ "@RULE.APurificationLevelOfMinusOneMeansNotUnlocked would have been retyped, though a"
		+ "change to either leaves the play untouched"
		REF @RULE.APlanetNumericIdIsStableAcrossSaves
		REF @RULE.APurificationLevelOfMinusOneMeansNotUnlocked
	REJECTED "Reading DOMAIN format as what a JSON Schema of"
		+ "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/ can refuse: it leaves a statement no"
		+ "single-save schema can check, such as an identifier being stable across saves, with no"
		+ "domain at all"
	SPEC "a RULE carries DOMAIN game only when a change to its statement would change how the game"
		+ "plays, and DOMAIN format when the statement can change with no consequence in play"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::FIELD DOMAIN format|game|merge"
	RATIONALE "The axis was derived three times before being settled: the 21 rules were typed once"
		+ "against no stated criterion, the verdict table that followed answered whether a"
		+ "statement was a merge rule, and the audit of the domains proposed a third reading. The"
		+ "criterion is recorded so the fourth derivation does not happen; applied to the 21 rules"
		+ "it confirms DOMAIN game at zero, the corpus having been extracted from a format document"
		+ "and a merge document"
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-18 on the audit of the 21 rules"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

DECISION AValueTableIsAJsonFileBesideTheModuleThatReadsIt
	SPEC "a product value table is a JSON array holding one row per line, with its JSON Schema"
		+ "beside it as <name>.schema.json, in the package whose module reads it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/energyLevels.schema.json"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/legacyTerrainLayerProperties.schema.json"
	SPEC "bun run validate:tables validates every table against its JSON Schema, each package"
		+ "naming its own tables in its own validate:tables script"
		IMPL "scripts/validate-tables.ts::findTableViolations"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/package.json::validate:tables"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/package.json::validate:tables"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/validate-tables.spec.ts"
	SPEC "the world object labels cover exactly the known world object names, which a spec asserts"
		+ "since the JSON import no longer types the keys"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/worldObjectLabels.spec.ts::should label no"
			+ "name the game is not known to use"
	REJECTED "one directory of tables at the repository root: each package would read outside its"
		+ "perimeter, and the root script would name paths inside the packages"
	REJECTED "keeping the label totality a type error through satisfies over a TypeScript literal:"
		+ "the literal is the second home of the rows the move removes"
	REJECTED "keeping the question on ProceduralWreckContainer1 as a comment beside its row: JSON"
		+ "carries no comment, so the question lives in its HYPOTHESIS alone, which names the label"
		+ "table"
		REF @HYPOTHESIS.ProceduralWrecksAreSpawnedByThePortalGenerator
		REF @DECISION.ACodeCommentQuestionNamesItsCorpusEntity
	REJECTED "keeping the source registry of the energy values as a markdown table: the page a"
		+ "value was read from is a column of its row, the source field"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE52
	RATIONALE "The module that reads a table owns it, so the JSON file sits beside that module and"
		+ "the import stays relative; the legacy terrain layer properties are read by no module and"
		+ "sit in shared-save-processing, which owns the wire format"
	SOURCE "ruled while delivering CHORE52, 2026-09-18"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
